To prevent direct path exchange between your BGP peers while maintaining the hub as the central communication point, use the `disable-client-reflect` command. This stops the route reflector from advertising routes between its clients. Apply it globally in BGP configuration mode:

```
system-view
bgp <your_AS_number>
 disable-client-reflect
 commit
```

Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your router's BGP autonomous system number. This configuration ensures all peers communicate exclusively through the hub without direct route exchanges.
