To address the issue of BGP path selection being influenced by IGP metrics, configure the router to ignore the next-hop metric in the BGP best path decision process:

```cli
system-view
bgp [as-number]
best-path-selection
ignore-nh-metric
```

**Steps explained:**  
1. Enter system view with `system-view`.  
2. Access BGP configuration using `bgp [as-number]` (replace `[as-number]` with your BGP AS).  
3. Navigate to the best-path selection context with `best-path-selection`.  
4. Disable IGP metric consideration using `ignore-nh-metric`.  

This ensures BGP no longer uses IGP distance (next-hop cost) when determining the best path.
