## User question:
Hey, so I'm troubleshooting some BGP link-state route info not updating properly from a neighbor (internal BGP, v4 address 192.168.100.5) on my Huawei NE40E. Instead of full resets, how do I gently nudge just the incoming routes from this specific peer to refresh without blowing up other sessions?
---
## Proposed answer:
To gently refresh incoming BGP link-state routes from the peer `192.168.100.5` without disrupting the session, use the following operational command:

```
refresh bgp ipv4 192.168.100.5 ls import
```

**Explanation:**  
- `refresh bgp`: Initiates a route refresh request.  
- `ipv4 192.168.100.5`: Specifies the IPv4 address of the peer.  
- `ls`: Targets the link-state address family.  
- `import`: Requests a refresh of **incoming** routes from the peer.  

This command triggers the peer to resend its BGP link-state routes without resetting the session, ensuring minimal disruption.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
refresh bgp link-state unicast { all | <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> | external | internal | group <group-name> } { export | import }
FuncDef:
The refresh bgp link-state unicast command softly resets a BGP-LS address family connection. BGP-LS address family soft reset can be used to refresh the BGP-LS address family routing table and apply new routing policies, without closing any BGP-LS address family connection.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'all', 'Info': 'All BGP connections.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a BGP peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'ipv6-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv6 address of a BGP peer.\nThe value is a 32-digit hexadecimal number, in the format of X:X:X:X:X:X:X:X.'}
{'Parameters': 'external', 'Info': 'Softly resets BGP connections.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'internal', 'Info': 'Softly resets IBGP connections.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'group group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a BGP peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'export', 'Info': 'Triggers outbound soft resetting.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'import', 'Info': 'Triggers inbound soft resetting.\n-'}
