## User question:
Working with a Huawei NE40E in a multi-cluster setup, when setting up BGP for layer 2 VPN auto-discovery, how do I adjust the route selection so the box cares more about the originating router's ID rather than those cluster group details when choosing the best path? Our current setup seems to ignore the source identifier hierarchy we want.
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust BGP route selection on your Huawei NE40E to prioritize the originating router's ID over cluster group details in a layer 2 VPN auto-discovery setup, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            no ignore-router-id
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures the router considers the originating router's ID during path selection by disabling the `ignore-router-id` parameter. By default, BGP compares router IDs when selecting paths, so this change enforces the desired behavior where the originating router's ID takes precedence over cluster-related attributes.
