## User question:
I’m working with a Huawei NE40E where a BGP neighbor at 2001:db8::1 is sending network topology info that includes internal codes 22 to 24 in the route details. What’s the best way to make the router drop or ignore any routes with those codes in their BGP-LS updates from this peer?
