## User question:
Hey, on Huawei NE40E devices, when using standard BGP for IPv4 traffic, what’s the trick to make the box automatically switch to pre-backed-up routes in the background so that if the primary path drops, the switch happens faster than a coffee sip? Our setup’s dual-homed but still stutters during outages.
---
## Proposed answer:
To achieve rapid failover to precomputed backup paths for IPv4 BGP routes on your dual-homed Huawei NE40E, configure BGP Fast Reroute (FRR) with backup paths:

```
configure router bgp
   backup-path ipv4
exit
```

This command precomputes backup paths for IPv4 prefixes. When the primary path fails, traffic immediately switches to the backup path without waiting for BGP reconvergence, minimizing outage impact.
