On a Huawei NE40E, trying to troubleshoot some path issues. How can I check the full list of network topology details that our box is grabbing from the device at 192.168.50.20 via BGP? Need to verify what's coming in.
---
## Proposed answer:
To check the full list of BGP routes received from the neighbor at 192.168.50.20, use the following operational command:  

```  
display bgp routing-table peer 192.168.50.20 received-routes  
```  

This command displays all routes received from the specified peer before inbound policy processing.  

If the neighbor session is not established, verify the neighbor configuration:  
```  
config  
router bgp  
 group <your-group-name>  
  neighbor 192.168.50.20  
```  

Ensure the neighbor IP is correctly configured under the appropriate BGP group.
