To optimize label allocation for VPNv6 routes sharing the same exit gateway and label on the Huawei NE40E, use the BGP add-paths capability to limit the number of paths advertised per prefix. This reduces label consumption by consolidating overlapping paths:

```cli
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        label-ipv6 send 1
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `label-ipv6 send 1` restricts the router to advertise only **1 path per VPNv6 prefix** to peers (down from a default of up to 16 paths). This ensures only one label is allocated per prefix, even when multiple paths exist to the same exit gateway.  
- By limiting path advertisements, overlapping routes share a single label, streamlining MPLS label allocation and reducing resource overhead.  

Apply this configuration globally under `bgp` to affect all VPNv6 routes, or refine it per BGP group/neighbor if needed.
