## User question:
Hey, on my Huawei NE40E, I need to manage the BGP link-state updates coming from a neighboring device at 192.168.50.45—what’s the best way to tweak the BGP-LS settings so it only accepts the network paths I want, using that "inbound-filter" rule set I already created?
---
## Proposed answer:
To manage BGP-LS updates from the neighbor at 192.168.50.45 and apply your existing "inbound-filter" rule set, use the following CLI commands:

```
config router bgp
 group <your-group-name>
  neighbor 192.168.50.45
   import route-policy inbound-filter
  exit
 exit
exit
```

Replace `<your-group-name>` with the BGP group containing this neighbor. This configuration applies your "inbound-filter" route policy to control accepted BGP-LS paths from 192.168.50.45.
