To ensure your Huawei NE40E router in ASN 65001 recognizes and advertises pre-existing default routes (0.0.0.0/0) via BGP, configure the following commands:

```
ip ip-prefix DEFAULT_ROUTE index 10 permit 0.0.0.0 0
!
route-policy IMPORT_DEFAULT permit node 10
 if-match ip-prefix DEFAULT_ROUTE
!
router bgp 65001
 rib-management
  ipv4
   route-table-import IMPORT_DEFAULT
  exit
 exit
```

This configuration:
1. Creates an IP prefix list (`DEFAULT_ROUTE`) matching the default route 0.0.0.0/0.
2. Defines a route policy (`IMPORT_DEFAULT`) that permits routes matching this prefix.
3. Enables BGP to import active default routes from the routing table into the BGP IPv4 RIB using `route-table-import`.

After applying these commands, BGP will advertise any active 0.0.0.0/0 routes from your routing table to peers. Verify with `display bgp routing-table 0.0.0.0` to confirm the route appears in BGP.
