To achieve sub-second BGP failover without relying on path preference attributes, configure BFD to detect link failures rapidly and tie BGP session state to the BFD session. Use these commands:

```
config>router>bgp
   group <primary_group_name>
      neighbor <primary_neighbor_ip>
         bfd-enable
      exit
   exit
exit
```

### Key points:
1. **`bfd-enable`** under the BGP neighbor binds the BGP session to the BFD session state
2. BFD detects link failures in milliseconds (adjust BFD timers on the interface for sub-second detection)
3. Ensure `disable-fast-external-failover` is **not** configured (default behavior enables fast failover)

> ⚠️ **Critical Pre-requisite**:  
> Configure BFD parameters on the physical interface first using:
