## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E box, I need to control which BGP Link-State topology routes get sent over to my IPv6 neighbor at 2001:DB8:2::2—specifically using a policy named LS-FILTER to block certain LS data. What’s the right way to tweak the config so only approved LS routes advertise, without exposing the rest?
---
## Proposed answer:
To control BGP Link-State topology routes to your IPv6 neighbor using the policy `LS-FILTER`, apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
  neighbor 2001:DB8:2::2
    export LS-FILTER
```

This ensures only routes permitted by the `LS-FILTER` policy are advertised to the neighbor `2001:DB8:2::2`, blocking all other LS data.
