User input:

Hey, on my Huawei NE40E, I’ve got a bunch of BGP VPNv4 routes coming in from a group of peers labeled "east_region" – need to make sure only the networks listed in "custA_routes" (which defines Customer A’s stuff) are accepted. Any quick way to tweak the config so it ignores everything else they’re sending?

To enable BGP to recognize up to eight backup paths for IPv6 unicast traffic on your Huawei NE40E, configure the following commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        ipv6 send 8 receive
    exit
    backup-path ipv6
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `ipv6 send 8 receive` command under `add-paths` enables BGP to advertise and receive **up to 8 paths** per IPv6 prefix for unlabeled unicast routes.  
- The `backup-path ipv6` command activates BGP Fast Reroute (FRR) for IPv6, allowing the router to use precomputed backup paths when primary paths fail.  

This configuration ensures BGP maintains multiple backup options (up to eight) for IPv6 unicast traffic and rapidly switches to them during failures.
