Based on your request to adjust the BGP link-state peer detection timer to 450 seconds, use the following CLI configuration commands. These modify the BGP graceful restart `restart-time` to the specified value, which controls how long the router waits for a peer to recover before declaring it down:

```cli
config
    router bgp
        graceful-restart
            restart-time 450
```

### Key details:
- **Context**: This is configured under the global BGP graceful restart settings, applying to all peers. For granular control (specific groups/neighbors):
  ```
  config>router>bgp>group <group_name> graceful-restart restart-time 450
  ```
  or
  ```
  config>router>bgp>group <group_name> neighbor <ip_address> graceful-restart restart-time 450
  ```
  
- **Effect**: Reduces the default 300-second wait time to 450 seconds, allowing faster detection of unresponsive BGP link-state peers during graceful restart scenarios.
