**Explanation:**  
- Enter `best-path-selection` configuration mode under BGP to modify path selection rules.  
- The `no ignore-router-id` command ensures the router ID comparison is **not skipped** during best path selection. This forces the router to evaluate the router ID (Step 10 in the BGP path selection process) before considering the cluster list (Step 11), as per standard RFC 4271 behavior.  

**Note:** Replace `<as-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number. This configuration applies globally to all address families, including VPNv4.
