## Proposed answer:
To enable automatic BFD for BGP-overlay tunnels on Huawei NE40E routers without manual session configuration, use the following CLI commands. This setup enables BFD at the BGP group level, applying it dynamically to all peers in the group:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <DYNAMIC_GROUP_NAME>
        dynamic-neighbor
        bfd-enable
```

**Explanation:**  
- Replace `<DYNAMIC_GROUP_NAME>` with your BGP group name for overlay tunnels.  
- `dynamic-neighbor` allows automatic discovery of BGP peers.  
- `bfd-enable` triggers BFD session establishment for all peers in the group, accelerating failure detection.  

BFD parameters (timers, etc.) are inherited from the underlying IP interface configuration. Ensure BFD is properly set up on the relevant interfaces.
