## User question:
Hey, I’m setting up an NE40E and need to make sure it shares those IPv6 segment IDs (you know, the ones tied to specific routes) with the BGP neighbor group "bgp_group1" when handling regular IPv6 traffic under BGP. What’s the trick to enable this in the right config mode?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable sharing IPv6 segment IDs with the BGP neighbor group "bgp_group1" for regular IPv6 traffic, use the following configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "bgp_group1"
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops label-ipv6
```

This command ensures labeled IPv6 routes are advertised with an IPv6 next-hop address to peers in the group when routes are originated or next-hop-self is applied.
