Based on your request to align IPv6 "no label" handling with IPv4 in BGP for 6PE, use the following configuration to ensure proper next-hop resolution and label inheritance:

```cli
configure router bgp
   next-hop-resolution
      labeled-routes
         transport-tunnel
            family label-ipv6
            exit
         exit
      exit
   exit
```

This configuration ensures that IPv6 labeled routes (`label-ipv6`) use the same next-hop resolution tunnel infrastructure as IPv4 routes. The key elements are:
- Activates the transport tunnel context for labeled IPv6 routes
- Inherits the same label handling rules (including reserved/implicit-null tags) as IPv4
- Resolves the path dropping issue by enforcing consistent label processing

For neighbor sessions where IPv6 routes are advertised, also verify that the `family ipv6 labeled-unicast` is properly configured under relevant BGP neighbors/groups.
