To address the issue of the Huawei NE40E dropping path tags too quickly during BGP-based label switching failover, configure the following commands to extend the retention of stale routes to approximately 30 seconds:

```
configure router bgp
graceful-restart
stale-routes-time 30
exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures temporary forwarding markers (stale routes) are maintained for 30 seconds during BGP reconvergence, allowing sufficient time for traffic rerouting around failed links.
