```cli
configure router bgp best-path-selection no ignore-router-id
```

**Explanation:**  
The `no ignore-router-id` command ensures the router compares BGP identifiers (router IDs) during best path selection. By default (`no ignore-router-id`), the router prioritizes lower router IDs in the best path decision before considering cluster-specific attributes. This configuration explicitly enforces router ID checks for all paths, including those influenced by cluster group markers.
