User input:

I’m setting up MPLS VPNs on a Huawei NE40E and noticed some routes from my BGP group "bgp_peers" aren’t sticking around after applying inbound filters. How do I force the router to keep every VPNv4 route it receives from this group, even if they don’t follow the rules I defined?

To address the route flips affecting MPLS label cleanup on your Huawei NE40E routers, configure the BGP stale routes timer to retain labels for 15 seconds after route withdrawal. Use these commands:

```
router bgp <your_AS_number>
 graceful-restart
  stale-routes-time 15
```

This setup preserves VPNv4 routes and associated labels during brief session interruptions, preventing premature label release and MPLS cleanup races. Ensure graceful restart is consistently configured across all BGP peers.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
