- **BGP group**: Apply under `config>router>bgp>group` to impact a specific peer group.
- **Individual neighbor**: Apply under `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor` for granular control.

**Example (global level):**
```
config>router>bgp
 local-preference 200
```

**Note:** This sets the local preference for routes when they are received by the reflector. If a route already has a local preference, this command will not override it unless applied with a route policy (not covered in the provided reference). Use a more specific level (group/neighbor) if you need targeted adjustments.
