## User question:
Hey folks, on Huawei NE40E routers handling BGP-driven LSPs with fast reroute, when a failover happens, how do I make the box wait a solid 15 seconds before flushing the old path's label mappings? Need that buffer to avoid traffic hiccups during flappy scenarios.
---
## Proposed answer:
To achieve a 15-second delay before flushing old label mappings after a BGP failover, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
  stale-routes-time 15
exit
```

This configures the router to maintain stale routes (including label mappings) for 15 seconds during graceful restart scenarios, providing the required buffer to prevent traffic disruptions during unstable conditions.
