To bundle the 172.16.64.0/18 network and suppress specific subnets while preserving AS path details, use the following configuration:

```cli
system-view
bgp <your_AS_number>
 ipv4-family unicast
  aggregate 172.16.64.0 18 as-set detail-suppressed
```

### Explanation:
- **`aggregate 172.16.64.0 18`**: Creates the summarized /18 route.
- **`as-set`**: Preserves the original AS path details (including AS_SET) from the more specific routes.
- **`detail-suppressed`**: Blocks advertisement of all more specific subnets (e.g., /19, /20) covered by the aggregate route.

Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your actual BGP AS number. This configuration ensures only the /18 aggregate is advertised while inheriting the AS path attributes of the suppressed subnets.
