## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E box handling multiple VPNs with BGP instances, I’ve got this internal BGP group called "bgp_vpn_grp" – how do I make sure when it shares routes within the group, the next-hop stays as the router’s own IP instead of getting swapped or inherited from elsewhere? Trying to prevent downstream hiccups here.
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure the next-hop remains the router's own IP for routes shared within the internal BGP group "bgp_vpn_grp", use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
  group bgp_vpn_grp
    next-hop-self
```

This command forces the router to advertise routes to all peers in the group using its local BGP address as the next-hop, overriding any inherited values and preventing downstream issues.
