## User question:
I'm setting up an MPLS service on a Huawei NE40E and noticed that BGP VPNv4 routes with labels aren't being prioritized properly when their next-hop resolution relies on LSPs. How do I tweak the config so these labeled routes can actually be considered when the box decides which path to use?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure BGP VPNv4 routes with labels prioritize LSPs for next-hop resolution, configure the following:

```cli
configure router
 bgp
  next-hop-resolution
   labeled-routes
    transport-tunnel
     family vpn
      resolution filter
      resolution-filter
       rsvp
      exit
     exit
    exit
   exit
  exit
 exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the VPN family context for BGP-labeled routes
2. Sets route resolution to use explicitly defined tunnel types (`filter`)
3. Enables RSVP LSPs as the transport tunnel type for next-hop resolution

The routes will now prioritize RSVP LSPs when resolving next hops for VPNv4 labeled routes.
