## User question:
Hey, I’m stuck with a Huawei NE40E setup where some BGP neighbors in an IPv6 group handling unicast updates seem sluggish—like their data arrives over 500 seconds late. What’s the trick to make the router flag those slowpoke peers causing the delay?
---
## Proposed answer:
To address sluggish BGP peers in your IPv6 group with unicast updates arriving over 500 seconds late, configure a lower hold time to force session resets for unresponsive neighbors. Use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
  group <group_name>
    hold-time 180
```

Replace `<group_name>` with your IPv6 BGP group name. This sets the hold time to 180 seconds (less than the 500-second delay threshold). Peers failing to send keepalives or updates within 180 seconds will be flagged as down, triggering session resets and alerting you to the unresponsive neighbors.
