## User question:
Hey, I'm setting up a Huawei NE40E where the BGP instance bgp200 needs to let an external neighbor group called remote_peers talk to it—problem is, some of these peers are way downstream through multiple intermediate devices. How do I tweak the config so it tolerates routing across up to 10 network jumps for these connections?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the Huawei NE40E for BGP instance bgp200 to allow the external group "remote_peers" to connect across up to 10 network hops, apply this command:

```
bgp 200
 group remote_peers external
  multihop 10
``` 

This sets the TTL value to 10 for the peer group, enabling BGP sessions with neighbors up to 10 hops away.
