To configure a 30-second hold-off period for BGP peer flapping in the "ISP_Backbone" group, use these commands:

```
bgp
 group ISP_Backbone
  hold-time 30
  keepalive 10
```

**Explanation:**  
- `hold-time 30` sets the maximum wait period to 30 seconds before declaring a peer down.  
- `keepalive 10` adjusts the keepalive interval to 10 seconds (required because BGP mandates `hold-time` ≥ 3 × `keepalive`).  

This ensures the router waits ~30 seconds after the last received message before reacting to peer failures. Apply this directly to the BGP group to affect all neighbors in "ISP_Backbone".
------------
