## User question:
Hey, on my Huawei NE40E, there's a BGP neighbor blasting too many routes at me—how do I force it to only accept the IPv4 networks I’ve pre-approved in a list named "bgp_filter" so they actually show up in the BGP table? Basically, I want to toss any routes not on that list before they get stored.
---
## Proposed answer:
To filter incoming BGP routes on your Huawei NE40E to only accept IPv4 networks in the "bgp_filter" list and discard others, configure the following commands directly under the specific BGP neighbor:

```cli
outbound-route-filtering
ip-prefix bgp_filter import
```

These commands enable outbound route filtering (ORF) and apply your "bgp_filter" prefix list to filter incoming routes from the neighbor. Only prefixes matching "bgp_filter" will be accepted into the BGP table; all others will be discarded before storage.
