To configure the BGP hold time to 200 seconds and enforce a minimum of 200 seconds for IPv6 neighbors on your Huawei NE40E, use the following commands. Replace `<GROUP_NAME>` and `<NEIGHBOR_IPv6_ADDRESS>` with your specific group and neighbor IPv6 address.

```
configure router bgp
 group <GROUP_NAME>
  neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IPv6_ADDRESS>
   hold-time 200 min 200
   keepalive 67
```

**Explanation:**  
- `hold-time 200 min 200` sets the hold timer to 200 seconds and forces the peer to accept at least 200 seconds (rejecting lower values).  
- `keepalive 67` adjusts the keepalive interval to ~1/3 of the hold time (200/3 ≈ 67 seconds), ensuring timely checks.  

Apply this configuration to all problematic IPv6 neighbors. If needed for an entire group, configure under `group <GROUP_NAME>` instead of per neighbor.
