Based on your requirement to adjust BGP path priority using a combined metric of external and internal factors, the following configuration implements this using BGP policies and attributes:

```cli
# Configure route policy to set custom metric
route-policy SET_WEIGHTED_METRIC
  apply cost-type internal
  apply cost (500 * med + 200 * igp-cost)
end-policy

# Apply policy to BGP neighbor
bgp 
  group <peer-group-name>
   neighbor <neighbor-ip>
    route-policy SET_WEIGHTED_METRIC import
    aigp
```

### Key components:
1. **`apply cost`** combines:
   - External metric (MED) multiplied by 500
   - Internal IGP metric multiplied by 200
2. **`aigp`** enables accumulation of IGP metrics
3. **`cost-type internal`** ensures proper metric calculation

This configuration modifies the path selection metric to prioritize routes based on your specified weighted formula during BGP best path selection. The neighbor-specific application ensures only routes from the target AS are affected.
