## User question:
On a Huawei NE40E, when dealing with BGP routes from a neighboring autonomous system, how can I adjust the path priority so that it combines the external metric (from their side) multiplied by 500 with our own internal path metric multiplied by 200? We’re trying to balance both factors but the usual methods aren’t giving the right weights.
---
## Proposed answer:
Based on your requirement to adjust BGP path priority using a combined metric of external and internal factors, the following configuration implements this using BGP policies and attributes:

```cli
# Configure route policy to set custom metric
route-policy SET_WEIGHTED_METRIC
  apply cost-type internal
  apply cost (500 * med + 200 * igp-cost)
end-policy

# Apply policy to BGP neighbor
bgp 
  group <peer-group-name>
   neighbor <neighbor-ip>
    route-policy SET_WEIGHTED_METRIC import
    aigp
```

### Key components:
1. **`apply cost`** combines:
   - External metric (MED) multiplied by 500
   - Internal IGP metric multiplied by 200
2. **`aigp`** enables accumulation of IGP metrics
3. **`cost-type internal`** ensures proper metric calculation

This configuration modifies the path selection metric to prioritize routes based on your specified weighted formula during BGP best path selection. The neighbor-specific application ensures only routes from the target AS are affected.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
bestroute med-plus-igp [ igp-multiplier <igp-multiplier> | med-multiplier <med-multiplier> ] *
undo bestroute med-plus-igp [ igp-multiplier <igp-multiplier> | med-multiplier <med-multiplier> ] *
FuncDef:
The bestroute med-plus-igp command enables BGP to use the sum of MED multiplied by a MED multiplier and IGP cost multiplied by an IGP cost multiplier to select routes when MED is required to determine the optimal route.
The undo bestroute med-plus-igp command restores the default configuration.
By default, the MED and IGP cost of each route are used as separate route selection criteria.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'igp-multiplier igp-multiplier', 'Info': 'Specifies an IGP cost multiplier.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 1000. The default value is 1.'}
{'Parameters': 'med-multiplier med-multiplier', 'Info': 'Specifies a MED multiplier.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 1000. The default value is 1.'}
