## User question:
Hey, when doing a major config overhaul on a Huawei NE40E, what’s the fastest way to make the box stop chatting with all its BGP neighbors at once instead of kicking them one by one? Trying to avoid downtime gaps during maintenance.
---
## Proposed answer:
To quickly stop all BGP neighbors simultaneously on your Huawei NE40E during maintenance, use the following command:

```
router bgp
 shutdown
```

This administratively disables the entire BGP process, immediately halting all neighbor sessions. When ready to restore, execute:

```
router bgp
 no shutdown
