Hey, I'm working on a Huawei NE40E box where I need to configure a bunch of internal BGP neighbors under the same VPN setup that uses multiple routing instances. How do I bundle these neighbors into a group called "core_peers" specifically for IPv4 stuff in that VPN environment without retyping the same parameters for each peer?

To control route advertisements to your BGP peer group "VPN_Clients" using ACL 2100, configure the following commands:

```
bgp
 group VPN_Clients
  peer VPN_Clients as-number [Peer-AS]
  peer VPN_Clients route-policy BLOCK_ACL_2100 export
#
route-policy BLOCK_ACL_2100 deny node 10
 if-match acl 2100
#
route-policy BLOCK_ACL_2100 permit node 20
#
```

Replace `[Peer-AS]` with the actual AS number of your VPN_Clients peers. This configuration:
1. Creates a route policy named `BLOCK_ACL_2100`
2. Uses ACL 2100 to block matching prefixes at node 10
3. Permits all other routes at node 20
4. Applies this policy to outbound advertisements to the VPN_Clients group

No existing route distribution will be disrupted as the policy explicitly permits non-matching routes.
