To balance incoming MPLS traffic across up to four equally-good BGP-learned label paths for entry-side tunnels on your Huawei NE40E, configure the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
   add-paths
      label-ipv4 send 4 receive
   exit
   best-path-selection
      ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv4
   exit
   ibgp-multipath
exit
```

### Key configurations explained:
1. **`label-ipv4 send 4 receive`**  
   Enables receiving and advertising up to four labeled-IPv4 paths per prefix for MPLS tunnel load balancing.

2. **`ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv4`**  
   Allows mixing EBGP and IBGP paths with the same metric to be considered equally for load balancing.

3. **`ibgp-multipath`**  
   Enables multipath load balancing for IBGP routes (required when using IBGP-learned paths).

This setup installs up to four equal-cost labeled paths into the routing table, enabling MPLS traffic balancing across entry-side tunnels. Ensure all BGP peers support the add-paths capability for seamless negotiation.
