To create a BGP peer group named "backbone" for internal neighbors and add peers to it, use the following CLI commands:

```
sys
bgp <AS-number>
group backbone
type internal
neighbor <ip-address1>
neighbor <ip-address2>
```

Replace `<AS-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number, and `<ip-address1>`, `<ip-address2>` with the actual IP addresses of your internal BGP neighbors. Add additional `neighbor` lines for each peer you want to include in the group.

This configuration:
- Creates a peer group called "backbone" under BGP
- Sets the group type to internal (iBGP)
- Inherits the internal type setting for all neighbors added to the group
- Eliminates the need to individually configure BGP type parameters for each peer
