Based on your request, the following CLI commands configure the router to conditionally apply recursive next-hop resolution only for routes in the `customer_routes_2023` filter. Non-customer routes will only resolve next-hops using directly connected routes, disabling multi-hop recursion.

```cli
/configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    policy customer_routes_2023
/configure router bgp next-hop-resolution shortcut-tunnel family ipv4
    resolution disabled
```

### Explanation:
1. **`policy customer_routes_2023`**:  
   This attaches the `customer_routes_2023` route policy to BGP next-hop resolution. Only routes permitted by this policy will be eligible for recursive next-hop resolution. Non-matching routes require direct next-hop reachability.

2. **`shortcut-tunnel family ipv4 resolution disabled`**:  
   Disables tunnel-based resolution (e.g., MPLS shortcuts) for IPv4 routes. Combined with the policy, this ensures non-customer routes only resolve through directly connected next-hops, while customer routes use standard recursive resolution as defined by the policy.
