To set a specific prioritization tag for IPv4 BGP routes based on the traffic selection list "customer123," configure a route-policy to apply the desired local-preference value. Use the following CLI commands:

```cli
route-policy customer123_policy permit node 10
 if-match extcommunity-filter customer123
 apply local-preference 200
 exit
!
bgp
 peer <neighbor_address>
 route-policy customer123_policy import
 exit
```

Replace `<neighbor_address>` with the appropriate BGP neighbor IP. This policy matches routes tagged with the "customer123" extcommunity filter and sets their local-preference to `200`. Adjust the `local-preference` value as needed for your prioritization requirements.
