To configure your Huawei NE40E to notify the neighbor at 192.168.50.25 of its ability to restart without dropping BGP connections, use the following CLI commands in the BGP configuration context. Replace `<group-name>` with the appropriate BGP group name and ensure you are in the correct BGP instance context.

```cli
group <group-name>
neighbor 192.168.50.25
graceful-restart
restart-time 300
long-lived
enable-notification
exit
exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`graceful-restart`**: Enables BGP Graceful Restart capability for the neighbor.
2. **`restart-time 300`**: Advertises a 300-second restart timer (default) to the neighbor, indicating how long routes should be preserved during a restart.
3. **`long-lived`**: Enables Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) to extend route retention beyond the standard timer if needed.
4. **`enable-notification`**: Allows graceful handling of NOTIFICATION messages, preventing session drops during events like maintenance.

This configuration ensures the neighbor at 192.168.50.25 retains routes and avoids session flapping during restarts or maintenance. Apply these commands under the relevant BGP group and neighbor context.
