To configure your Huawei NE40E to accept only specific networks from neighbor 192.168.50.20 using the prefix list `cust-a-routes`, apply the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    neighbor 192.168.50.20
        import "cust-a-routes"
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
This configuration applies the `cust-a-routes` policy to inbound routes from the neighbor 192.168.50.20. The policy must be pre-configured under `policy-options` to permit the allowed prefixes and deny all others. Only routes matching the `cust-a-routes` policy will be accepted; all other prefixes from this peer will be blocked.
