To configure the BGP keepalive and hold timers for the neighbor 192.168.50.25, use the following commands:

```cli
peer 192.168.50.25
 keepalive 15
 hold-time 45
```

**Explanation:**  
- `keepalive 15` sets the interval for sending keepalive messages to **15 seconds**.  
- `hold-time 45` sets the maximum wait time before declaring the peer down to **45 seconds**.  

Ensure these commands are applied within the BGP neighbor configuration context (under `bgp [as-number] > peer 192.168.50.25`). The values satisfy the BGP requirement (hold-time ≥ 3 × keepalive interval).
