---
## User question:
Working on a Huawei NE40E where BGP paths from different AS peers in a VPNv4 instance might get evaluated differently based on when they arrive—how can I set it up so the router always picks the same best route, no matter the order they’re learned?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure consistent BGP best-path selection in your VPNv4 instance regardless of the order routes are learned, configure deterministic MED comparison:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        deterministic-med
```

This groups paths by neighbor AS before MED comparison, making path selection order-independent. The router will always evaluate MED consistently across different AS peers.
