To share the BGP link-bandwidth extended community with all neighbors in the `cust123` group at once, use these commands:

```cli
configure
router bgp
group cust123
 link-bandwidth
  send-to-ebgp ipv4
 exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`group cust123`**: Enters the configuration context for the BGP group `cust123`.
2. **`link-bandwidth`**: Enables handling of the link-bandwidth extended community for all neighbors in this group.
3. **`send-to-ebgp ipv4`**: Specifies that the link-bandwidth extended community will be attached to IPv4 routes advertised to all EBGP neighbors in `cust123`.

This configuration applies the settings to the entire group, eliminating the need to configure individual neighbors. Replace `ipv4` with other address families (e.g., `ipv6`) if required by your setup.
