## User question:
Hey, working on a Huawei NE40E setup where I've got several routers grouped as "internal_peers" in a private network segment (VPN instance). They keep automatically linking via BGP even though I don't want that—tried tweaking the usual route policy stuff but no luck. Any way to force the NE40E to just ignore BGP handshakes with this whole crew in that virtualized environment?
