## Proposed answer:
To prevent your Huawei NE40E from establishing BGP sessions with the "internal_peers" group in the VPN instance, administratively disable the BGP group. Use the following CLI commands:

```cli
config
 service
  vprn <vprn_instance_name>
   bgp
    group internal_peers
     shutdown
    exit
   exit
  exit
 exit
```

Replace `<vprn_instance_name>` with your specific VPN instance name. This will disable all BGP peering attempts with the entire group while preserving your configuration settings.
