To trust all route advertisements from the external neighbor 192.168.50.25 and skip the first-hop network ID check in BGP, configure the following:

```
configure terminal
router bgp
 group EXTERNAL_GROUP
  neighbor 192.168.50.25
   next-hop-unchanged
   exit
  exit
 exit
exit
commit
```

**Explanation:**  
The `next-hop-unchanged` command disables modification of the next-hop attribute for routes received from the specified neighbor. This bypasses the standard BGP validation that expects the next-hop to match the neighbor's address, allowing routes with arbitrary next-hop information to be accepted. This is applied directly to the neighbor `192.168.50.25` under a dedicated BGP group.
