User input:

Hey, I'm working on a Huawei NE40E and need to set up a BGP neighbor cluster called "group1" to recognize their network identifier as 300—like, where exactly do I slot in that 300 value in the group settings? Trying to avoid mismatched handshakes with another network here.

To assign the group identifier (cluster ID) 192.168.1.100 and prevent reflection loops for VPNv4 routes, configure the cluster ID at the BGP group level:

```cli
configure
router bgp <AS-number>
 group <group-name>
  cluster 192.168.1.100
```

Replace `<AS-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number and `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP peer group. This configuration designates 192.168.1.100 as the cluster ID for route reflection, preventing update loops by avoiding redundant route advertisements within the same cluster.
