To add the device at 192.168.50.20 to the existing BGP group "VPN_PEERS" on your Huawei NE40E, use the following commands:

```bash
router bgp
 group VPN_PEERS
  neighbor 192.168.50.20
```

This configures the specified IP as a static BGP peer under the "VPN_PEERS" group. Existing group-level settings (like address families or policies) will automatically apply to this new neighbor. The configuration preserves current sessions while adding the new peer.
