To configure BGP for continuous neighbor liveness checks with a 30-second delay before route changes, use the following commands:

```
system-view
bgp <your_as_number>
 peer 192.168.5.5 as-number <neighbor_as_number>
 peer 192.168.5.5
  keepalive 10
  hold-time 30
```

**Explanation:**  
- `keepalive 10` sends BGP keepalive messages every 10 seconds for rapid detection.  
- `hold-time 30` waits 30 seconds (half a minute) after missing keepalives before declaring the neighbor down and triggering route changes.  

This ensures quick detection (10-second intervals) while preventing flapping by enforcing a 30-second stabilization delay before route updates.
