peer <ipv4-address> as-number <as-number>
undo peer <ipv4-address>
FuncDef:
The peer as-number command creates a peer or configures an AS number for a specified peer group.
The undo peer as-number command deletes a specified peer or the AS number of a specified peer group.
By default, no BGP peer is configured, and no AS number is specified for a peer or peer group.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'as-number', 'Info': 'Specifies a destination AS number.\nFor an integral AS number, the value is an integer ranging from 1 to 4294967295.\nFor an AS number in dotted notation, the value is in the format of x.y, where x and y are integers ranging from 1 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively.'}
