User input:

I'm setting up a Huawei NE40E and want to make sure only specific network paths from our "customer_routes" list get shared with our BGP neighbor at 192.168.50.20—how do I tweak the config to check the origin AS details before sending updates to that peer?

To configure the BGP group WEST_GROUP to source its traffic from 192.168.50.1 for peers, use these commands:

```
router bgp
 group WEST_GROUP
  dynamic-neighbor
   prefix 192.168.50.1/32
  exit
 exit
!
```

