To configure the Huawei NE40E to manage path information shared with the neighbor at 192.168.50.25 using the specified list 2100 for blocking certain advertisements, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <your-group-name>
        neighbor 192.168.50.25
            outbound-route-filtering
                extended-community
                    send-orf 2100
```

**Notes:**  
- Replace `<your-group-name>` with the actual BGP group name where the neighbor is configured.  
- Ensure the list `2100` is a valid extended community policy (route-target based) for filtering.  
- These commands enable sending an ORF (Outbound Route Filter) to the peer at 192.168.50.25, blocking advertisements based on the extended community policy `2100`.
