On a Huawei NE40E, during a network upgrade where I need to avoid session drops during planned maintenance, what steps are needed to tell all neighbors in the BGP cluster named "bgp_grp1" that the router supports restarting smoothly without interrupting their connections?

To make BGP paths without a MED value less preferred by treating them as having the highest possible MED (infinity), use this configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            always-compare-med infinity
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This ensures routes without a MED are treated as having a MED of `4294967295` (infinity), making them the least preferred during path selection.
