## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E, when BGP is picking between paths that have MED values and some that don’t, how do you make the router slap the biggest possible MED on the ones without it so they’re less preferred?
---
## Proposed answer:
To make BGP paths without a MED value less preferred by treating them as having the highest possible MED (infinity), use this configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            always-compare-med infinity
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This ensures routes without a MED are treated as having a MED of `4294967295` (infinity), making them the least preferred during path selection.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
bestroute med-none-as-maximum
undo bestroute med-none-as-maximum
FuncDef:
The bestroute med-none-as-maximum command configures BGP to assign the maximum MED (4294967295) to a route without MED in route selection.
The undo bestroute med-none-as-maximum command restores the default configuration.
By default, BGP assigns 0 to a route without MED.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
