To configure the BGP aggregation as requested, use the following commands:

```cli
system-view
bgp <your_AS_number>
 ipv4-family unicast
  aggregate 192.168.64.0 18 as-set detail-suppressed attribute-policy FLTR_MAIN
```

### Explanation:
1. **`aggregate 192.168.64.0 18`**: Creates a summarized route for the `/18` prefix (192.168.64.0/18).
2. **`as-set`**: Preserves the original AS path groupings by including all AS numbers from the more specific routes in an AS_SET attribute.
3. **`detail-suppressed`**: Suppresses advertisements of the underlying smaller prefixes (prevents leaking more specific routes).
4. **`attribute-policy FLTR_MAIN`**: Applies your custom route-policy to modify attributes (e.g., communities, local-preference) of the aggregated route.
