To configure the BGP group "internal_peers" with a shared ASN of 65001 for all members, use the following commands:

```cli
router bgp
 group internal_peers
  peer-as 65001
  type internal
```

This configuration:
1. Creates the BGP group named `internal_peers`.
2. Sets the peer ASN to `65001` for all group members (applies to every peer in the group).
3. Designates the peers as internal (iBGP), ensuring they use the same ASN.

After applying this group configuration, add individual peers under the group using the `neighbor <ip-address>` command (no need to set ASN individually). For example:
```cli
 group internal_peers
  neighbor 192.168.1.1
  neighbor 192.168.1.2
```
