To capture all route advertisements from the "bgp_peers" neighbor group before inbound policy evaluation on your Huawei NE40E, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
router bgp
 group bgp_peers
  peer <peer_ip> log-update receive
```

Replace `<peer_ip>` with the specific peer IP address(es) in the group. Repeat the `peer` command for each BGP peer in the group.  

**Important notes**:  
1. This configuration logs every received BGP update from the peer before any inbound policy processing.  
2. Logs can be viewed using `display bgp peer <peer_ip> log-info`  
3. For persistent logging, ensure adequate storage/logging settings  
4. Apply this configuration temporarily during troubleshooting as it generates significant logs  

For the entire neighbor group, apply this to each peer individually as group-level logging commands aren't supported in this context.
