To set the timer so it doesn't wait longer than 500 seconds for the "all routes synced" signal from peer 192.168.5.5, configure the `stale-routes-time` for that neighbor:

```
configure router bgp
  neighbor 192.168.5.5
    graceful-restart
      stale-routes-time 500
    exit
  exit
exit
```
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Hey, on Huawei NE40E boxes, if the BGP process is restarting and needs to wait for peer 192.168.5.5 to send that "all routes synced" signal, how do I set the timer so it doesn’t hang around longer than 500 seconds waiting for that confirmation? Trying to avoid stale waits after a session reset.
---
## Proposed answer:
To set the timer so it doesn't wait longer than 500 seconds for the "all routes synced" signal from peer 192.168.5.5, configure the `stale-routes-time` for that neighbor:

```
configure router bgp
  neighbor 192.168.5.5
    graceful-restart
      stale-routes-time 500
    exit
  exit
exit
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib <time-value>
undo peer <ipv4-address> graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib
FuncDef:
The peer graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib command sets the maximum duration for a BGP restarter to wait for the End-of-RIB flag from a specified peer.
The undo peer graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib command deletes the configured duration.
By default, a BGP restarter waits for the End-of-RIB flag from a specified peer for a maximum of 600s.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a BGP peer.\nThe value is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'time-value', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum duration for a BGP restarter to wait for the End-of-RIB flag.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 3 to 3000, in seconds.'}
