To prevent the Huawei NE40E from modifying the next-hop attribute in BGP updates sent over the broadcast-style L2 tunnel link, apply the following configuration:

1. **At the BGP group level** (if all neighbors in the group require this behavior):
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
   next-hop-unchanged
```

2. **At the specific neighbor level** (if only certain neighbors require this):
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip>
   next-hop-unchanged
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the neighbor's IP address. This ensures BGP advertises routes without altering the next-hop attribute to directly attached peers on the broadcast segment.
