## User question:
Hey, we’ve got a Huawei NE40E box that needs to share only specific networks from our "custA-routes" list when talking BGP with a peer at 192.168.50.30—how do we lock it down so it doesn’t spill the beans on other routes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure only specific networks from "custA-routes" are shared with the BGP peer at 192.168.50.30, configure outbound route filtering at the neighbor level:

```cli
neighbor 192.168.50.30
  outbound-route-filtering
exit
```

This enables BGP outbound route filtering for the peer, restricting advertised routes to only those specified in your filter lists.
