CLIs:
peer <group-name> fake-as <fake-as-value> [ dual-as ] [ prepend-global-as ] [ prepend-fake-as ]
undo peer <group-name> fake-as
FuncDef:
The peer fake-as command enables a device to use a fake AS number to establish a BGP peer relationship with a specified peer.
The undo peer fake-as command cancels the existing configuration.
By default, a device uses an actual AS number to establish a BGP peer relationship with a peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'fake-as fake-as-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a destination AS number.\nFor an integral AS number, the value is an integer ranging from 1 to 4294967295.\nFor an AS number in dotted notation, the value is in the format of x.y, where x and y are integers ranging from 1 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively.'}
{'Parameters': 'dual-as', 'Info': 'Allows the local end to use the actual or fake AS number to establish a BGP peer relationship with the specified peer.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'prepend-global-as', 'Info': 'Indicates that the actual AS number is added to packets to be sent.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'prepend-fake-as', 'Info': 'Indicates that the fake AS number is added to received packets.\n-'}
