## User question:
If a link suddenly drops in my Huawei NE40E's BGP-based customer VPN (IPv4), how do I get it to automatically switch to backup paths right away—without waiting for the usual route recalculation dance? Trying to steer clear of those BGP attributes that track path capacity for this.
---
## Proposed answer:
To achieve immediate switchover to backup paths for your BGP-based customer VPN (IPv4) without relying on path capacity tracking, use the following configuration:

```cli
config>router>bgp
    backup-path label-ipv4
```

This enables BGP fast reroute for labeled IPv4 routes, allowing traffic to divert to precomputed backup paths instantly upon primary path failure, bypassing standard BGP convergence delays. Ensure your VPN prefixes have multiple paths advertised to utilize this feature.
