## User question:
Hey, I’ve got a Huawei NE40E that’s having trouble with a BGP neighbor at 192.168.50.45 because they’re using one of those really big AS numbers that’s longer than the old two-byte ones. The session keeps flapping—how do I tweak the config so the router recognizes and processes these extended ASNs correctly?
