## Proposed answer:
To resolve the BGP session flapping issue with the neighbor at 192.168.50.45 using a 4-byte AS number, configure the following commands. Ensure you are in the correct BGP neighbor configuration context (whether directly under `router bgp` or within a group):

```cli
configure
router bgp
 neighbor 192.168.50.45
  no disable-4byte-asn
```

**Important notes:**
1. If the neighbor is part of a BGP group, first enter the group configuration before the neighbor context:
   ```cli
   group <your-group-name>
    neighbor 192.168.50.45
     no disable-4byte-asn
