On a Huawei NE40E, I’m trying to make sure a route policy named "customer_routes" stops certain internal routes from being advertised to our transit providers. How can I apply this policy to the BGP group "transit_peers" to control what’s sent out to those peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To apply the route policy "customer_routes" to the BGP group "transit_peers" and control outbound advertisements to transit providers, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
bgp <as-number>
 group transit_peers
  export customer_routes
```

Replace `<as-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number. This configuration applies the "customer_routes" policy to filter outbound routes advertised to all peers in the "transit_peers" group.
