To adjust the maximum segment size to 300 bytes for BGP peers in the "internet_peers" group, use the following configuration commands:

```cli
group internet_peers
 peer tcp-mss 300
```

This sets the TCP maximum segment size to 300 bytes for all peers in the "internet_peers" group during session establishment.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Hey, I’ve got a Huawei NE40E handling multiple VPN routing tables for IPv4, and I need to tweak how it connects to my external BGP neighbors labeled “internet_peers.” The problem is, when these sessions initialize, the TCP handshake seems to carry oversized packets—I want to clamp down the maximum segment size to 300 bytes specifically for these peers in that multi-VPN setup. How do I adjust that parameter without breaking the existing config?
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the maximum segment size to 300 bytes for BGP peers in the "internet_peers" group, use the following configuration commands:

```cli
group internet_peers
 peer tcp-mss 300
```

This sets the TCP maximum segment size to 300 bytes for all peers in the "internet_peers" group during session establishment.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> tcp-mss <tcp-mss-number>
undo peer <group-name> tcp-mss
FuncDef:
The peer tcp-mss command configures a TCP MSS value used when the local device establishes TCP connections with a peer group.
The undo peer tcp-mss command deletes the configured TCP MSS value.
By default, no TCP MSS is configured for the local device to establish TCP connections with a peer group.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'tcp-mss-number', 'Info': 'Specifies the TCP MSS value used for TCP connection establishment.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 176 to 4096, in bytes.'}
