Based on your request to restrict BGP to using only the immediate next-hop for routes passing the "bgp_filter123" filter while preventing recursive lookups for other paths, configure the following:

```
config router bgp
 next-hop-res
  no use-bgp-routes
```

This globally disables BGP recursive next-hop resolution. Since the default behavior already avoids recursive lookups, this command explicitly enforces direct next-hop usage for all routes, including those that pass your filter. For routes requiring recursive resolution, ensure they are explicitly handled through separate routing policies or tunnel configurations not covered in your filter constraint.
