To add the note "NY_Backbone_Link" to your BGP neighbor at 192.168.50.2, use these CLI commands:

```cli
configure
router bgp
 neighbor 192.168.50.2
  description "NY_Backbone_Link"
 exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `neighbor 192.168.50.2` command enters the configuration context for the specified peer.  
- The `description` command attaches your note directly to this neighbor.  
- Quotes (`" "`) are used around the description string to ensure special characters/spaces are handled correctly.  

This adds the label directly to the BGP session configuration.
