I’m working on a Huawei NE40E where I need to stop a specific neighbor (192.168.50.25) from forming a BGP connection, even though we’re juggling multiple VPN setups—any clever way to tweak the config so it outright rejects this peer without breaking the other VPN relationships?
---
## Proposed answer:
To block the BGP neighbor 192.168.50.25 while preserving other VPN relationships, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.168.50.25
            shutdown
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the relevant BGP group name where the neighbor is configured. This administratively disables the specific neighbor without impacting other peers or VPN configurations.
