To configure the Huawei NE40E as a silent listener for the BGP peer at 192.168.50.20 (only responding to connection requests and never initiating), use the following commands:

```
group <your-group-name>
neighbor 192.168.50.20
passive
```

Replace `<your-group-name>` with the appropriate BGP group name. This configures the router to operate in passive mode for the specified neighbor, ensuring it only responds to incoming connections and does not initiate sessions.
