To configure your Huawei NE40E router to accept BGP updates from neighbor `192.168.1.5` that include your AS number up to three times in the AS_PATH without blocking them, apply the following command at the neighbor level:

```cli
configure router
 bgp
  group <your_group_name>
   neighbor 192.168.1.5
    loop-detect off
   exit
  exit
 exit
exit
```

Replace `<your_group_name>` with the BGP group name where the neighbor is configured. This disables loop detection for `192.168.1.5`, allowing routes with repeated AS numbers to be accepted normally.
