User input:

I’m troubleshooting a site-to-site route exchange issue on a Huawei NE40E. In the BGP setup under the address family that handles VPN targets, how can I make sure VPNv4 and VPNv6 routes aren’t blocked by the peer’s import targets? I need them to pass through without checking those specific filters.

To prevent route bouncing and loops for the BGP neighbor at 203.179.24.55 with the site-specific tag, configure the following:

```cli
config>router>bgp
    neighbor 203.179.24.55
        loop-detect discard-route
    exit
exit
```

This configuration discards routes containing the local AS in the AS path, preventing loops while maintaining the BGP session. For optimal route reflection using the site-specific tag 172.16.25.30:80, ensure the location ID is defined under BGP optimal route reflection and assigned to the neighbor as a route reflector client. For example:

```cli
config>router>bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location <location-id> primary-ip-address 172.16.25.30
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<location-id>` with a valid value (1-16). Then, associate the neighbor with this location as a route reflector client.
