This configuration discards routes containing the local AS in the AS path, preventing loops while maintaining the BGP session. For optimal route reflection using the site-specific tag 172.16.25.30:80, ensure the location ID is defined under BGP optimal route reflection and assigned to the neighbor as a route reflector client. For example:

```cli
config>router>bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location <location-id> primary-ip-address 172.16.25.30
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<location-id>` with a valid value (1-16). Then, associate the neighbor with this location as a route reflector client.
