To ensure the NE40E does not drop any BGP routes received from the neighbor 192.168.50.2, regardless of inbound policy matches, configure the router to disable the acceptance of ORF (Outbound Route Filtering) filters from this peer. This prevents the peer from imposing filters that may affect route retention.

```cli
configure router bgp
    neighbor 192.168.50.2
        outbound-route-filtering
            extended-community
                no accept-orf
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation**:  
- **`outbound-route-filtering`** and **`extended-community`** enter the necessary configuration contexts.  
- **`no accept-orf`** ensures the router does not accept any ORF-based filters from the peer (192.168.50.2), overriding any inbound filtering rules imposed by the peer.  

This configuration allows all received routes from 192.168.50.2 to remain in the routing table.
