To configure automatic route summarization for the VPN instance "vpnb" on your Huawei NE40E, use the following commands in BGP configuration mode:

```
ipv4-family vpn-instance vpnb
 aggregate <summary-network> <mask> detail-suppressed
```

Replace `<summary-network>` and `<mask>` with the appropriate summarized network address and subnet mask. The `detail-suppressed` keyword ensures only the summary route is advertised while suppressing more specific routes. 

For example, to summarize `192.168.1.0/24`, `192.168.2.0/24`, and `192.168.3.0/24` into `192.168.0.0/16`:

```
ipv4-family vpn-instance vpnb
 aggregate 192.168.0.0 255.255.0.0 detail-suppressed
```

Ensure the summarized range covers all local routes you want to bundle. The routes must exist in the local VPN routing table before aggregation occurs.
