To set the reconnect wait time for the BGP neighbor at 192.168.50.2 to 45 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
router bgp [as-number]
 group [group-name]
  peer 192.168.50.2
   connect-retry 45
```

**Explanation:**  
- Replace `[as-number]` with your BGP autonomous system number.  
- Replace `[group-name]` with the BGP group containing the neighbor.  
- The `connect-retry 45` command sets the reconnect timer directly for the specified neighbor.  

**Note:**  
If the neighbor is in a virtual routing instance (VRF), first enter the VRF context under BGP:  
```cli
router bgp [as-number]
 vrf [vrf-name]
  group [group-name]
   peer 192.168.50.2
    connect-retry 45
```
