To resolve the BGP packet fragmentation issue with neighbor 192.168.55.66 and enable automatic path MTU discovery, configure the following commands:

```
config
  router bgp
    group <your_group_name>   # Replace <your_group_name> with the appropriate peer group
      neighbor 192.168.55.66
        path-mtu auto-discovery
```

### Key points:
1. The `path-mtu auto-discovery` command enables automatic detection of the maximum packet size to prevent fragmentation.
2. This configuration must be applied within the BGP neighbor context under the relevant peer group.
3. Replace `<your_group_name>` with the actual BGP peer group name where the neighbor is configured.

The router will now dynamically determine the optimal MTU for BGP updates to 192.168.55.66 without requiring manual MTU adjustments.
