To enable automatic prefix-based route adjustments with your BGP peer at 192.168.10.5 using outbound route filtering (ORF), apply these CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group ORF_GROUP
            peer 192.168.10.5
                outbound-route-filtering
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `outbound-route-filtering` enables dynamic prefix-list synchronization for both inbound/outbound routes.  
- ORF automatically exchanges and updates prefix filters with the peer at 192.168.10.5 when routes change.  
- No manual prefix-list adjustments are needed after this configuration.  

> **Note:** Ensure the peer IP is already configured under a BGP group. Replace `ORF_GROUP` if the peer exists in a different group.
