## Proposed answer:
To configure the BGP path preferences as requested, use the following CLI commands. Replace `<external-group-name>` and `<internal-group-name>` with your actual BGP group names, and `<as-number>` with your BGP AS number.

```cli
configure
router bgp <as-number>
 group <external-group-name>
  preference 10
 exit
 group <internal-group-name>
  preference 15
 exit
exit
```

**Notes**:  
- These commands set the administrative distance for routes learned from external peers to `10` and internal peers to `15` at the group level.  
