To prevent labeled summary routes from leaking into VPN routing tables on your Huawei NE40E, configure the following command under BGP:

```cli
configure
router bgp
    disable-route-table-install
``` 

This stops all BGP routes (including labeled IPv4 summaries) from installing into the base routing table, preventing their unintended propagation into VPN instances.
