To apply the "customer_filter" policy to outbound BGP updates for the neighbor at 192.168.50.25, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
config>router>bgp
group <your_group_name> 
 neighbor 192.168.50.25
  outbound-route-filtering
   extended-community
    send-orf
```

**Explanation:**  
This configuration enables outbound route filtering (ORF) with extended community support and activates the `send-orf` capability for the specified neighbor. The "customer_filter" policy (which must be defined as an extended community policy) will automatically be used to control which routes are advertised to 192.168.50.25. The `send-orf` command ensures the router negotiates ORF capabilities with the peer to enforce the policy-based filtering.
