## User question:
I'm trying to secure BGP sessions over IPv6 on a Huawei NE40E and want the router to act as the server side for encrypted handshakes when talking to a neighbor at 2001:db8::1 – how do I set this up where our box initiates the SSL/TLS setup instead of just using plain TCP?
---
## Proposed answer:
To secure BGP sessions over IPv6 with encrypted handshakes on the Huawei NE40E router, configure the router as the TLS server for the neighbor `2001:db8::1`. Use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group_name>
            neighbor 2001:db8::1
                local-address <your_local_ipv6_address>
                tcp-authentication tls server
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key parameters to replace**:
- `<group_name>`: Your BGP group name.
- `<your_local_ipv6_address>`: The IPv6 address of your router's interface used for the BGP session.

**Note**:  
- The `tcp-authentication tls server` command enables TLS encryption with the router acting as the server (initiating the handshake).
- Ensure TLS certificates and keys are properly configured on the router for the encryption handshake to succeed.
- IPv6 BGP address-family configuration (e.g., `family ipv6`) must be enabled separately under the neighbor/group if not already active.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer { <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> } ssl-policy role server
peer { <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> } ssl-policy role client
peer { <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> } ssl-policy role disable
undo peer { <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> } ssl-policy role server
undo peer { <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> } ssl-policy role client
undo peer { <ipv4-address> | <ipv6-address> } ssl-policy role disable
FuncDef:
The peer ssl-policy role client command configures a peer as an SSL client.
The undo peer ssl-policy role client command cancels the SSL client configuration.
The peer ssl-policy role server command configures a peer as an SSL server.
The undo peer ssl-policy role server command cancels the SSL server configuration.
The peer ssl-policy role disable command disables SSL role setting for a peer.
The undo peer ssl-policy role disable command restores the default configuration and takes effect only when the peer ssl-policy role disable command is run.
By default, no peer is configured as an SSL client or server.
