To make routes from the BGP neighbor 192.168.1.2 more preferred with a priority of 75, apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure
    router bgp
        group <your-group-name>  # Replace <your-group-name> with the appropriate BGP group
        neighbor 192.168.1.2
            preference 75
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
The `preference 75` command sets the administrative distance for routes received from neighbor 192.168.1.2 to 75. Since a lower administrative distance (e.g., 75) is preferred over higher values (default BGP preference is 170), this ensures routes from this neighbor are prioritized during path selection. Existing policies remain unaffected as the change is localized to this specific neighbor.
