To address the issue of BGP pausing route recalculations due to an unstable next-hop in the "vpn2" VPN, disable BGP route damping. This prevents BGP from suppressing updates during gateway instability:

```cli
configure service vprn vpn2
    bgp
        no damping
    exit
exit
```

This command globally disables route damping for all BGP neighbors within the "vpn2" VPN instance. Routes will now propagate immediately regardless of next-hop flapping. If you need to disable damping for a specific neighbor or group instead, use:

```cli
configure service vprn vpn2
    bgp
        group <GROUP_NAME>
            neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP>
                no damping
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<GROUP_NAME>` and `<NEIGHBOR_IP>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP address.
