To block incoming routes from neighbor 192.168.55.66 using the predefined filter `bgp_filter123`, configure the following commands:

```bash
configure router bgp
  group <your-group-name>
    neighbor 192.168.55.66
      outbound-route-filtering
        extended-community
          accept-orf
```

Replace `<your-group-name>` with the BGP group name where the neighbor is configured. This enables accepting Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) from the neighbor, allowing the locally configured `bgp_filter123` to be applied to incoming routes.
