1. Replace `<your-group-name>` with the actual BGP group name where the neighbor 192.168.5.2 is configured.  
2. `compare-origin-validation-state` ensures BGP evaluates route legitimacy (Valid/Not-Found/Invalid) during best-path selection.  
3. `extended-community` under the neighbor's outbound-route-filtering advertises the origin validation state directly to 192.168.5.2.  

This configuration will flag suspicious routes and propagate the validation results to the specified peer.
