To ensure the most optimal external path details are shared with the internal BGP neighbor at 192.168.10.5 in a redundant setup, configure Optimal Route Reflection (ORR) with the following commands:

```cli
bgp <your_as_number>
 optimal-route-reflection
  location 1 primary-ip-address 192.168.10.5
 exit
 peer 192.168.10.5 reflect-client
 peer 192.168.10.5 location 1
```

Replace `<your_as_number>` with your BGP autonomous system number. This configuration:
1. Defines a location ID (1) for the route reflector using the neighbor's IP as the primary address
2. Configures the neighbor as a route reflector client
3. Assigns the location ID to the neighbor 

The router will now calculate and advertise optimal external paths specific to this neighbor's location while maintaining existing peer relationships.
