To prioritize BGP VPNv4 routes by assigning the worst metric to routes lacking a default metric (MED), use the `local-preference` command to set the lowest possible value (0) for routes without the local preference attribute. This ensures such routes are deprioritized during path selection. Apply this configuration at the BGP instance level:

```cli
system-view
bgp <your_AS_number>
 local-preference 0
commit
```

Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your actual BGP autonomous system number. This forces routes without local preference to use 0 (least preferred) during BGP best path selection, effectively nudging traffic away from them when alternatives exist.
