To set up BGP updates from 192.168.5.2 across multiple virtual routing setups without leaking paths between overlapping networks, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
router bgp <as-number>
   neighbor 192.168.5.2
      outbound-route-filtering
         extended-community
            send-orf
         exit
      exit
   exit
exit
```

### Key Details:
1. **`outbound-route-filtering`**: Enables BGP Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) for the neighbor to dynamically exchange route filters.
2. **`extended-community`**: Specifies ORF based on Extended Communities (Route Targets).
3. **`send-orf`**: Automatically sends locally configured Route Targets to the peer (192.168.5.2), ensuring only relevant VPN routes are exchanged. This prevents route leaks between overlapping VRFs by filtering updates based on negotiated Route Targets.

Replace `<as-number>` with your BGP AS number. This configuration ensures the peer only sends routes matching your local VRFs' import targets, eliminating path leakage.
