Based on your request to disable the safety check blocking recursive lookups for IPv6 unicast routes due to next-hop flapping, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-res
 no use-bgp-routes
exit
```

This command disables BGP route recursion globally for both IPv4 and IPv6, allowing direct handling of next-hop instability without recursive blocking. If you need to re-enable recursion later, replace `no use-bgp-routes` with `use-bgp-routes`.
