- The command `no disable-client-reflect` enables route reflection for clients in the group "internet_peers." By default (`no disable-client-reflect`), routes learned from one client in this group are reflected to other clients, allowing indirect route exchange through the router. This avoids the need for a full mesh between external BGP neighbors.
