## User question:
Hey, I’m setting up BGP for IPv6 on a Huawei NE40E and need paths from external AS neighbors to actually evaluate those MED numbers properly—right now it’s ignoring them when the peers are in different ASNs. What config tweaks do I need under the IPv6 unicast part to force it to start comparing those MEDs cross-AS?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable MED comparison across different AS neighbors for IPv6 BGP, apply the following configuration:

```cli
router bgp
 best-path-selection
  always-compare-med zero
```

This forces BGP to evaluate MED values from all external AS peers during path selection, treating routes without MED as 0.
