To configure your Huawei NE40E to advertise the 192.168.10.0/24 network using the `CUSTOM_POLICY` ruleset while preserving existing peer configurations, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0
    export "CUSTOM_POLICY"
```

**Key details:**  
- The `network` command ensures BGP advertises the 192.168.10.0/24 prefix.  
- The `export` command applies your pre-defined `CUSTOM_POLICY` to control how this route is pushed to **all BGP peers** at the global BGP level.  
- If `CUSTOM_POLICY` contains special characters (e.g., spaces, `#`, `$`), double quotes are required.  

> **Note:**  
> - If a global export policy already exists, this command will **replace** it. To preserve existing policies, combine them with `CUSTOM_POLICY` into a new unified policy first.  
> - The `export` command affects all peers unless overridden at the group/neighbor level. Existing peer-specific policies remain unchanged.  
> - Ensure `CUSTOM_POLICY` is correctly defined in `config>router>policy-options` to permit 192.168.10.0/24.
