To configure the router to wait 7.5 minutes (450 seconds) before switching to the backup route when the primary BGP session fails, use the following command on the primary BGP neighbor:

```
hold-time 450 min 450
```

This sets the BGP hold timer to 450 seconds and ensures the peer also accepts a minimum hold time of 450 seconds. Apply this under the specific neighbor or group configuration for the primary link. For example:

```
bgp
 group primary_group
  peer 192.0.2.1
   hold-time 450 min 450
   quit
  quit
 quit
```
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Hey, on Huawei NE40E boxes, if there's a main line and a fallback, how can I make the router wait like 7 and a half minutes before deciding to use the backup route when the primary flickers? Trying to avoid flapping when the main link has short hiccups.
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the router to wait 7.5 minutes (450 seconds) before switching to the backup route when the primary BGP session fails, use the following command on the primary BGP neighbor:

```
hold-time 450 min 450
```

This sets the BGP hold timer to 450 seconds and ensures the peer also accepts a minimum hold time of 450 seconds. Apply this under the specific neighbor or group configuration for the primary link. For example:

```
bgp
 group primary_group
  peer 192.0.2.1
   hold-time 450 min 450
   quit
  quit
 quit
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
route-select delay <delay-value>
undo route-select delay
FuncDef:
The route-select delay command configures a route selection delay.
The undo route-select delay command deletes the configured route selection delay.
