## User question:
Hey, I'm working with a Huawei NE40E and need to tweak BGP so when it shares OSPF routes (from the instance labeled 65001) with another network, it only lets through the ones allowed by a policy I created called OSPF_FILTER. How do I hook that filter into BGP’s outbound route advertisements properly?
---
## Proposed answer:
To apply the OSPF_FILTER policy for outbound BGP advertisements of redistributed OSPF instance 65001 routes, configure the following:

```
configure
 router bgp <your_as_number>
  peer <neighbor_ip_address>
   export route-policy OSPF_FILTER
  exit
 exit
```

Replace `<your_as_number>` with your BGP autonomous system number and `<neighbor_ip_address>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This attaches the policy directly to the neighbor for outbound route filtering.  

If applied to a BGP group instead:
```
configure
 router bgp <your_as_number>
  group <group_name>
   export route-policy OSPF_FILTER
  exit
 exit
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
route-filter <route-filter-name> { import | export [ direct | isis <process-id> | ospf <process-id> | rip <process-id> | static ] }
undo route-filter <route-filter-name> { import | export [ direct | isis <process-id> | ospf <process-id> | rip <process-id> | static ] }
FuncDef:
The route-filter export command filters the routes to be advertised so that BGP advertises only desired routes.
The undo route-filter export command restores the default configuration.
The route-filter import command filters the routes to be received.
The undo route-filter import command restores the default configuration.
By default, received routes or the routes to be advertised are not filtered.
