- **`peer-as <neighbor-AS>`**: Replace `<neighbor-AS>` with the neighbor's actual AS number to establish the BGP session.
- **`remove-private skip-peer-as`**: Removes all private AS numbers from advertised routes except the neighbor's AS (preserving their non-public AS).

### Requirements:
1. Replace `<your-group-name>` with your BGP group name.
2. Replace `<neighbor-AS>` with the neighbor's autonomous system number.
3. This configuration applies specifically to the neighbor at 192.168.50.25.
