To configure your Huawei NE40E as a transparent BGP route passer for the external neighbor 192.168.50.45, use these commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
  group <your_group_name>
    neighbor 192.168.50.45
      no local-preference
      no aggregator-id-zero
    exit
  exit
exit
```

**Key notes:**
- Replace `<your_group_name>` with the actual BGP group name where the neighbor is configured
- `no local-preference` ensures the router doesn't modify the LOCAL_PREF attribute
- `no aggregator-id-zero` prevents alteration of the aggregator path attribute
- These settings disable attribute manipulation while maintaining default route propagation behavior

Apply this configuration directly to the specific neighbor to override any group-level or global BGP settings.
