To set up encrypted BGP sessions using SSL/TLS certificates for the neighbor at 192.168.5.20, configure the following commands:

```
config>router>bgp
 group <your-group-name>
  neighbor 192.168.5.20
   ssl-policy <your-ssl-policy-name>
```

**Note**:  
- Replace `<your-group-name>` with your BGP group name.  
- Replace `<your-ssl-policy-name>` with your predefined SSL policy configured with certificates.  
- Ensure the SSL policy (including certificate settings) is configured separately in the system context.  

