## User question:
On a Huawei NE40E, I’ve got some IPv6 routes coming into BGP from another protocol, and I need to tweak the metric that makes other networks think twice before sending traffic our way—specifically setting it to 500. How do I pull that off?
---
## Proposed answer:
To set the MED to 500 for IPv6 routes redistributed into BGP on your Huawei NE40E, use the following configuration commands:

```cli
bgp <your_AS_number>
 med-out 500
```

Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your actual BGP autonomous system number. This command applies the MED value of 500 to routes advertised to BGP peers when the MED is not already set.
