To prioritize voice and critical data traffic using the "traffic_priority" route-filter and set QoS markers via BGP, configure the following:

```cli
route-policy traffic_priority_policy
  if route-filter traffic_priority then
    set local-preference 200
  endif
exit

configure router bgp
  group <your_group_name>
    neighbor <neighbor_IP>
      import policy traffic_priority_policy
    exit
  exit
exit
```

Replace `<your_group_name>` and `<neighbor_IP>` with your BGP group name and neighbor IP address. This policy applies a higher local preference (200) to routes matching the "traffic_priority" filter, ensuring prioritized traffic handling.
