To verify if IPv6 routes from `2001:DB8:300::/48` are correctly imported into BGP, configure a route policy to match the specific prefix and apply it to BGP IPv6 RIB management. Use these commands:

```cli
ip ipv6-prefix STATIC_ROUTE_IPV6 index 10 permit 2001:DB8:300::/48
!
policy
 policy-statement IMPORT_STATIC_IPV6
  entry 10
   from
    ipv6-prefix STATIC_ROUTE_IPV6
   accept
  exit
 exit
!
router bgp <AS_Number>
 rib-management
  ipv6
   route-table-import IMPORT_STATIC_IPV6
   exit
  exit
 exit
```

After applying this configuration, check the BGP IPv6 routing table with:
```cli
display bgp ipv6 routing 2001:DB8:300::/48
``` 
This confirms if the static route is active in BGP.
