Hey, on my Huawei NE40E box running the "BGP_Backbone" process, I need to check all the VPNv4 paths that are currently being throttled because they’ve been unstable lately—can I get a list showing which ones are suppressed and how many flaps they’ve had?

To view suppressed or delayed IPv6 VPN routes in the "corp_network" VPN on your Huawei NE40E, use the following BGP configuration commands to ensure inactive routes are advertised and IPv6 next hops are properly set:

```huawei
configure router bgp
  group <your_group_name>
    neighbor <neighbor_IP>
      advertise-inactive
      advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6
    exit
  exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `advertise-inactive` forces BGP to advertise routes even if they are inactive.  
- `advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6` ensures VPNv6 routes use IPv6 next hops.  

After applying these, use `display bgp vpnv6 routing-table` to inspect routes. Replace `<your_group_name>` and `<neighbor_IP>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor details.
