On a Huawei NE40E, when troubleshooting multicast traffic, how can I view the BGP category 5 updates (specifically the ones related to live source discovery) that have been sent over to neighbor 172.16.25.40?
---
## Proposed answer:
To view the BGP category 5 updates (for live source discovery) sent to neighbor `172.16.25.40` on a Huawei NE40E, use the following command:  

```  
display bgp mvpn peer 172.16.25.40 advertised-routes  
```  

This command displays all MVPN routes (including **category 5 Source Active AD routes**) advertised to the specified neighbor. Look for entries labeled **"Source Active"** in the output to identify live source discovery updates.  

**Note**: Ensure the MVPN address family is properly configured between the peers for this output to populate.
