To monitor unstable IPv6 routes with AS paths starting with 65001 followed by any number, use the following command to view route flapping statistics:  

```  
display bgp routing-table ipv6 flap-info as-path-filter <filter-name>  
```  

First, define an AS path filter to match the required pattern. Create the filter using:  

```  
ip as-path-filter <filter-name> permit "65001_[0-9]+"  
```  

Then execute the `display bgp routing-table ipv6 flap-info` command with the filter to show only the unstable prefixes matching the AS path pattern.
