To ensure consistent IPv6 BGP best path selection on Huawei NE40E routers that factors in link bandwidth and avoids path flapping due to advertisement order, use the following configuration:

```cli
config>router>bgp
 group <GROUP_NAME>
  link-bandwidth
   send-to-ebgp ipv6
   aggregate-used-paths ipv6
exit
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`link-bandwidth`** enables bandwidth-based path selection
2. **`send-to-ebgp ipv6`** attaches link-bandwidth metrics to IPv6 routes advertised to EBGP peers
3. **`aggregate-used-paths ipv6`** ensures consistent bandwidth aggregation during route readvertisement

Replace `<GROUP_NAME>` with your BGP peer group. This configuration:
- Uses actual link bandwidth as a deterministic path selection factor
- Eliminates dependency on route advertisement timing
- Maintains consistency after reboots or peer resets
- Automatically propagates bandwidth metrics through the network

For neighbor-specific configurations, apply the same `link-bandwidth` settings under individual neighbors instead of the group.
------------
