To view the live status and detailed setup for the BGP neighbor `10.20.30.40` in your multicast over BGP setup, use the following commands:

```cli
display bgp multicast peer 10.20.30.41 verbose
```
**Details verified**:  
- Session state (Established/Down), uptime, negotiated capabilities  
- Address families activated (e.g., `ipv4 multicast`)  
- Received/advertised routes, flap statistics  
- Graceful restart/long-lived timer status  

```cli
display bgp multicast routing-table peer 10.20.30.41
```
**Details verified**:  
- Active multicast distribution trees (`(S,G)` or `(*,G)` entries)  
- Next-hop interfaces, route attributes (e.g., origin, MED, AS path)  
- Route selection status (valid/best)  

```cli
display pim routing-table
```
**Details verified**:  
- Multicast tree state (Join/Prune) downstream of BGP next-hop  
- RPF interface toward `10.20.30.41` (critical for tree connectivity)  

```cli
display multicast rpf-info source-address 10.20.30.41
```
**Details verified**:  
- RPF route source (BGP-learned) and metric  
- Failover paths (if any)  

> **Note**: Replace `10.20.30.41` with your neighbor IP. Use `verbose` in the first command for capabilities/timers. The outputs confirm neighbor liveliness, multicast route propagation, and distribution tree health.
