To prevent new BGP neighbors from auto-activating IPv4 traffic routing, configure the neighbors in passive mode. This stops the router from initiating sessions until you manually enable them. Here are the commands:

```
bgp <as-number>
  group <group-name>
    neighbor <ip-address>
    passive
```

When ready to activate IPv4 routing, disable passive mode:
```
bgp <as-number>
  group <group-name>
    no passive
```
