## User question:
Hey, on our Huawei NE40E boxes, after a recent code update, we need to make sure a BGP neighbor group named "internet_peers" can't handle the bigger AS numbers anymore. How do we tweak the config to roll back to the classic ASN format for those peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the BGP group "internet_peers" to use classic 2-byte AS numbers, apply this command:

```bash
router bgp
 group internet_peers
  disable-4byte-asn
```

This command disables 4-byte ASN support for all peers in the "internet_peers" group, enforcing the classic ASN format.
