User input:

I'm troubleshooting on a Huawei NE40E and need to see what IPv6 VPN routes via BGP were pushed to neighbor 203.0.113.45 for the 2001:db8:abcd::/64 block, including any subprefixes under it—how do I confirm exactly what's being shared there?

To view all multicast VPN path entries from neighbor 10.20.30.40 via BGP, including bandwidth-related flags, apply the following configuration:

```cli
configure terminal
router bgp
 neighbor 10.20.30.40
  link-bandwidth
  add-paths
   mvpn-ipv4 send 1 receive
   mvpn-ipv6 send 1 receive
  exit
 exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`link-bandwidth`**: Enables processing of the link-bandwidth extended community for routes received from the neighbor.
2. **`mvpn-ipv4 send 1 receive`**: Negotiates to receive multiple multicast VPN IPv4 paths per prefix (add-paths capability).
3. **`mvpn-ipv6 send 1 receive`**: Negotiates to receive multiple multicast VPN IPv6 paths per prefix (add-paths capability).

After applying this configuration, use these operational commands to view the details:
```cli
display bgp mvpn all routing-table path-attribute
display bgp mvpn-ipv6 all routing-table path-attribute
display bgp mvpn all peer 10.20.30.40 received-routes
display bgp mvpn-ipv6 all peer 10.20.30.40 received-routes
```
