Hey, on a Huawei NE40E, I’ve got a VPN setup handling IPv4 routes for a client. How do I tweak the “local preference” to 150 specifically for routes learned via that external protocol (you know, the one that connects different networks) within their virtual routing instance’s config? Need to prioritize a certain path without messing up existing policies.
---
## Proposed answer:
To set the local preference to 150 for BGP-learned routes in a specific VPN instance on the Huawei NE40E, use the following CLI commands:

```
bgp <as_number>
ipv4-family vpn-instance <vpn_instance_name>
local-pference 150
```

Replace `<as_number>` with your BGP AS number and `<vpn_instance_name>` with the name of your VPN instance. This configuration applies the local preference value directly to all routes learned via BGP within the specified VPN instance, ensuring path prioritization without affecting other policies.
