The configuration commands to set up a BGP peer group and neighbor for multicast VPNs on the Huawei NE40E are as follows:

```cli
config
router bgp
 group <name>
  neighbor <ip-address>
```

**Parameters:**  
- Replace `<name>` with the peer group name (up to 32 characters; enclose in double quotes if using special characters).  
- Replace `<ip-address>` with the BGP peer's IPv4 address.  

To view status details for update group ID 1024, use the operational command:  
```cli
display bgp update-group group-index 1024
```  

This command displays real-time status and configuration details for the specified update group to troubleshoot route distribution issues.
