To configure the BGP group "WEST_REGION" with autonomous system number 65001 (65k1) on your Huawei NE40E, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
router bgp
group WEST_REGION
 peer-as 65001
```

This sets the AS number for all peers in the "WEST_REGION" group to 65001. If you haven't created the group yet, the `group WEST_REGION` command will automatically create it. To add specific neighbors to this group, use the `neighbor <ip-address>` command under the group context.
