To configure the Huawei NE40E to share route markers like bandwidth hints with the multicast VPN peer group "mvpn_peers," use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
group "mvpn_peers"
link-bandwidth
send-to-ebgp ipv4
exit
exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
These commands enable the `link-bandwidth` extended community for IPv4 routes within the BGP group "mvpn_peers." The `send-to-ebgp ipv4` directive ensures bandwidth hints are attached to IPv4 routes advertised to all peers in this group, allowing neighbors to recognize and utilize them for traffic adjustments.
