## User question:
I'm setting up a BGP neighbor group called "backbone_peers" on our Huawei NE40E box and want to hardcode a numeric tag (64) for all members to influence path preferences - how do I stick that fixed value to the group instead of per-neighbor?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a fixed preference value of 64 for all members of the BGP neighbor group "backbone_peers," use the following commands:

```
router bgp
 group backbone_peers
  preference 64
```

This sets the route preference at the group level, applying the value uniformly to all peers in the group.
