To ensure the router passes custom tagging values (like traffic steering tags) to all peers in the "l2vpn_group1" BGP neighbor group, configure the `link-bandwidth` extended community under the group and enable it for the appropriate address family. Use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
 group "l2vpn_group1"
  link-bandwidth
   send-to-ebgp ipv4
  exit
 exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `link-bandwidth` command enters the configuration context for handling extended communities (e.g., traffic steering tags).  
- `send-to-ebgp ipv4` enables the router to advertise the `link-bandwidth` extended community to all EBGP peers in the group for IPv4 routes. Replace `ipv4` with the relevant address family (e.g., `l2vpn`) if your VPN setup uses non-IPv4 routes.  

This configuration attaches the extended community to routes advertised to peers in "l2vpn_group1," allowing downstream traffic engineering without modifying existing VPN policies.
