## User question:
I’ve got a Huawei NE40E setup where I need to log every VPNv6 BGP route advertisement from my peer group "bgp_peers" for troubleshooting, even if those routes get rejected by the inbound rules. How do I force the router to keep a copy of all these updates, approved or not, in the VPNv6 table?
---
## Proposed answer:
To log all VPNv6 BGP route advertisements from the peer group "bgp_peers," including routes rejected by inbound rules, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    mp-bgp-keep
```

This command forces the router to retain all MP-BGP routes in the RIB-IN table, ensuring all VPNv6 advertisements from peers are preserved regardless of inbound policy acceptance.
