To block unwanted BGP updates for customer VPN routes and only allow those in the "client-routes" list, use the following configuration:

```cli
# Create prefix list and route policy
policy-options
 begin
  prefix-list "client-routes" [Specify allowed prefixes]  # e.g., 192.168.1.0/24, 10.1.0.0/16
  route-policy "allow-client-routes" permit node 10
   if destination in prefix-list "client-routes" then
    accept
   endif
  !
  route-policy "allow-client-routes" deny node 20   # Implicit deny-all after node 10
  commit
 end

# Apply policy to BGP neighbor
router bgp [AS-number]
 group [group-name]   # Or configure directly under neighbor
  neighbor [peer-IP-address]
   family vpnv4
    export policy "allow-client-routes"
```

### Key details:
1. **prefix-list "client-routes"**: Define your allowed VPN routes here
2. **route-policy**: 
   - Node 10 permits routes matching the prefix-list
   - Node 20 implicitly blocks all other routes (default deny)
3. **export policy**: Applied to VPNv4 address family to filter outbound updates

Replace bracketed values `[ ]` with your specific parameters. This ensures only routes in "client-routes" are advertised to the customer peer.
