To list the specific BGP MVPN AD entries using the third key type (Shared Tree Join, Type 6) pointing to the shared tree at 172.16.1.5, use this CLI command:

```bash
display bgp mvpn routing-table type 6 | include 172.16.1.5
```

### Explanation:
- **`type 6`**: Filters routes to show only **Shared Tree Join (Type 6)** entries.
- **`| include 172.16.1.5`**: Further narrows the output to entries containing the shared tree address **172.16.1.5** (e.g., RP address).

This command will display only the Type 6 MVPN routes associated with the shared tree at 172.16.1.5.
