Based on your requirements, use the following CLI configuration to limit the distribution of VPN routes with a specific route-target to a maximum of 8 external BGP neighbors:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group EXTERNAL_GROUP
        type external
        family vpnv4
        neighbor <neighbor_ip_1>
        neighbor <neighbor_ip_2>
        ... (repeat for up to 8 neighbors)
        exit
    exit
    route-target-list target:<as_number>:<value>
    outbound-route-filtering
        extended-community
            route-target-list target:<as_number>:<value>
            send-orf
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**  
1. Create a dedicated BGP group (`EXTERNAL_GROUP`) containing **exactly 8 neighbors**. Replace `<neighbor_ip_1>`, `<neighbor_ip_2>`, etc., with the actual neighbor IPs.  
2. Define the specific route-target using `route-target-list target:<as_number>:<value>`.  
3. Enable `outbound-route-filtering` with `send-orf` to enforce that **only this group** receives routes matching the specified route-target.  

This configuration ensures that VPN routes carrying the defined route-target community will only be advertised to the explicitly configured neighbors in `EXTERNAL_GROUP`, effectively capping distribution at 8 peers.
