Hey, I’ve got a Huawei NE40E where I need to put a hold on the BGP neighbor relationships tied to a specific neighbor group named prod_servers during maintenance, but I don’t want to nuke their configs entirely. How can I just put those sessions to sleep for a bit without erasing their settings?

To view the paths learned from the peer at 172.16.1.1 with the extended community 65001:200, use the following CLI command:

```
display bgp routing-table peer 172.16.1.1 received-routes | include 65001:200
```

### Explanation:
- **`display bgp routing-table peer 172.16.1.1 received-routes`** shows all BGP routes received from the peer at 172.16.1.1.
- **`| include 65001:200`** filters the output to display only routes containing the extended community `65001:200`.

This command will confirm whether these routes appear in the BGP routing table. If no routes are displayed, they are not being received or accepted from the peer.
