To troubleshoot laggy IPv6 routes and verify BGP neighbor performance in your "corp_network_vrf" VPN setup, configure BGP monitoring for VPN-IPv6 neighbors:

```
service
 vprn "corp_network_vrf"
  bgp
   group <your_group_name>
    neighbor <neighbor_IPv4_address>
     family vpn-ipv6
      monitor
      exit
     exit
    exit
   exit
  exit
 exit
```

Replace `<your_group_name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor_IPv4_address>` with the specific neighbor's IPv4 address. This enables VPN-IPv6 monitoring for the neighbor, allowing you to track throughput and path attributes.

To check all configured VPN-IPv6 neighbors in the VRF, use:
```
display bgp vpnv6 vpn-instance corp_network_vrf peer
```
