---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the timer for waiting up to 200 seconds for BGP neighbors to send the End-of-RIB signal after a BGP process restart on the Huawei NE40E, use the `stale-routes-time` command under the graceful restart configuration. This sets the maximum time stale routes are retained while awaiting the "all routes done" signal.

Apply the configuration globally for all neighbors:
```cli
configure router bgp graceful-restart
 stale-routes-time 200
exit
```

For specific BGP groups or neighbors, configure it under the relevant hierarchy:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group_name> graceful-restart
 stale-routes-time 200
exit
```
or
```cli
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <neighbor_ip> graceful-restart
 stale-routes-time 200
exit
``` 

Ensure graceful restart is enabled for this configuration to take effect.
