## Proposed answer:
```
peer remote_peers enable
peer remote_peers keep-all-routes
```

**Explanation:**  
The `peer <group-name> enable` command activates the peer group, while `peer <group-name> keep-all-routes` ensures the router retains **all received BGP routes** from peers in the group, including routes rejected by inbound policies. This allows full visibility into advertised routes even if they are filtered.
