To view the BGP VPNv4 routes from neighbor 192.168.1.100 with specific route target tags, temporarily configure a global route target filter. After viewing the routes, remove the filter to restore normal operation.

**Configure the route target filter:**
```
configure
router bgp
 route-target-list <comm-id>
```

**After viewing the routes, remove the filter:**
```
configure
router bgp
 no route-target-list
```

Replace `<comm-id>` with your route target (e.g., `target:100:100`). Use standard `display` commands (e.g., `display bgp vpnv4 all routing-table peer 192.168.1.100`) to view the filtered routes between these configurations.  

**Note:** This temporarily restricts accepted VPNv4 routes to those matching the specified route target(s). Ensure this doesn’t disrupt production traffic.
