To apply the "customer_filter" route policy for exporting specific VPN routes to the "remote_group" BGP peers, use the following configuration:

```cli
system-view
bgp <your_as_number>
 group remote_group
  ipv4-family vpnv4
   peer remote_group enable
   peer remote_group route-policy customer_filter export
```

Replace `<your_as_number>` with your local BGP AS. This configuration:
1. Enters BGP configuration mode
2. Selects your peer group "remote_group"
3. Configures in VPNv4 address family
4. Enables the peer group for VPNv4
5. Applies "customer_filter" as an export policy to control advertised routes

For VPNv6 routes, use the same structure in `ipv6-family vpnv6` view. Ensure "customer_filter" is properly configured to match your desired VPN routes before applying.
