## User question:
I'm setting up a Huawei NE40E to share its preferred external route picks with internal BGP neighbors in the "internal_peers" group—how do I adjust the config so they reliably receive these optimal paths without breaking existing peer relationships?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure your Huawei NE40E shares its preferred external route selections with internal BGP neighbors in the "internal_peers" group, enable the best-external route advertisement globally in BGP configuration mode:

```cli
configure router bgp
    advertise-external
exit
```

This command ensures the router advertises its best external route to the destination even when the overall best route is an internal path. It applies to all supported address families (IPv4, IPv6, labeled-unicast) by default. The "internal_peers" group must already be configured with `type internal` to maintain proper peer relationships, but no additional group-level changes are needed.
