To configure BGPv6 peering to accept only specific IPv6 routes from your client using the "customer-routes-v6" list, apply this configuration:

```cli
config router bgp
    group <your_group_name>
        neighbor <client_IPv6_address>
            outbound-route-filtering
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key notes:**  
1. Replace `<your_group_name>` with your BGP group name and `<client_IPv6_address>` with the client's IPv6 address  
2. Ensure the prefix-list "customer-routes-v6" is already configured on your router to match the client's approved IPv6 routes  
3. This configuration enables Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) to enforce route acceptance strictly based on the locally configured "customer-routes-v6" prefix list  

Apply these commands in the appropriate BGP neighbor context to enforce the route filtering policy.
