## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP for your "NYC_BRANCH" group on the Huawei NE40E, ensuring routes always use this router's interface IP as the next-hop, use the following commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "NYC_BRANCH"
        next-hop-self
    exit
exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`next-hop-self`** forces all advertised routes to use a local BGP interface IP as the next-hop, overriding any inherited values.
2. This applies to all route types (including L2VPN) and both EBGP/IBGP peers in the group.

Regarding the local port's speed details:  
