To create the "customer_filter" for screening IPv6 BGP paths based on AS hops without extended communities, use an AS path filter and apply it to the BGP group:

```cli
ip as-path-filter customer_filter deny <AS_hop_regex>
ip as-path-filter customer_filter permit .*
!
bgp
 group asia_group
  ipv6-family
   import as-path-filter customer_filter
  exit
 exit
exit
```

Replace `<AS_hop_regex>` with a regular expression matching the AS sequences you want to block (e.g., `_1234_` for AS1234 transit). The filter will deny paths containing the specified AS hops and permit all others.
