As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
When setting up MVPN over BGP on a Huawei NE40E box, I'm trying to limit what multicast path info gets pushed to my "mvpn-peers" neighbor cluster. How do I hook up that "mvpn-filter" rule list I made to screen outgoing advertisements specifically for these peers? Basically want to block certain tree branches from being shared while letting others through.
---
## Proposed answer:
To limit MVPN advertisements to your "mvpn-peers" group using the "mvpn-filter" policy, configure the following:

```cli
bgp [AS number]
  group mvpn-peers
    export mvpn-filter
    vpn-apply-export
```

Replace `[AS number]` with your BGP autonomous system. This applies the export policy "mvpn-filter" to screen outgoing MVPN routes for the specified peer group, blocking unwanted multicast tree branches while permitting others.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> route-policy <route-policy-name> export
undo peer <group-name> route-policy <route-policy-name> export
FuncDef:
The peer route-policy export command specifies a route-policy for filtering routes to be advertised to a peer group.
The undo peer route-policy export command deletes a specified route-policy.
By default, no route-policy is configured for the routes to be advertised to a specified BGP peer group.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of an BGP peer group.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported.'}
{'Parameters': 'route-policy-name', 'Info': 'The name is a string of 1 to 200 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 200 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported.'}
{'Parameters': 'export', 'Info': 'Applies a route-policy to routes to be advertised to a peer group.\n-'}
