To scrub internal-only AS numbers from the BGP path for the "L2VPN_GROUP" peers, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
 group "L2VPN_GROUP"
  remove-private
```

This command removes all private AS identifiers from the AS path before advertising routes to peers in the group. No optional parameters like `limited` or `skip-peer-as` are included, ensuring all non-public ASNs are stripped regardless of position or peer ASN.
```console
config>router>bgp
group backbone-peers
preference 200
exit
exit
```

