To configure the Huawei NE40E to use the "internet_routes" route list for filtering outbound BGP advertisements to your global partners group, use these CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
  group global_partners
    export internet_routes
```

**Explanation:**  
1. `configure router bgp` enters BGP configuration mode.  
2. `group global_partners` accesses the BGP group for your global partners (replace `global_partners` with your actual group name).  
3. `export internet_routes` applies the "internet_routes" policy to control advertised routes to this peer group.  

Ensure the "internet_routes" policy is already defined in `config>router>policy-options` with appropriate filtering rules. This configuration will screen advertised routes exclusively for the specified peer group.
