To enable BGP path MTU discovery for the "europe_branches" peer group, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "europe_branches"
        path-mtu-discovery
    exit
exit
```

This setting automatically adjusts the TCP MSS to avoid fragmentation across varying MTU paths by leveraging ICMP messages and the DF bit.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Hey, on our Huawei NE40Es, how do I make BGP automatically figure out the max packet size it can use without breaking stuff when talking to our "europe_branches" peer group? These peers connect offices across different countries where MTU might vary.
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP path MTU discovery for the "europe_branches" peer group, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "europe_branches"
        path-mtu-discovery
    exit
exit
```

This setting automatically adjusts the TCP MSS to avoid fragmentation across varying MTU paths by leveraging ICMP messages and the DF bit.
---
