## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> keep-all-routes
undo peer <group-name> keep-all-routes
FuncDef:
The peer keep-all-routes command saves all the BGP routing updates from the specified peer or the peer group after the BGP connection is set up, even though those routes do not pass the configured ingress policy.
The undo peer keep-all-routes command disables this function.
By default, only the BGP routing updates received from the peer group and passing the configured ingress policy are saved.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
---
Please answer Correct or Incorrect.
Your answer:

```cli
configure
  router
    bgp
      group WEST_REGION
        prefix-limit ipv4 50000 threshold 80 idle-timeout forever
```

### Explanation:
1. **`group WEST_REGION`**: Enters configuration context for the BGP peer group "WEST_REGION".
2. **`prefix-limit ipv4 50000`**: Sets a maximum limit of 50,000 IPv4 path entries (routes) from the group.
3. **`threshold 80`**: Triggers a syslog warning (scream bloody murder) when paths reach 80% of the limit (40,000 paths).
4. **`idle-timeout forever`**: Automatically tears down the BGP peering ("nukes itself") if the limit is exceeded, requiring manual intervention to restore the session. No automatic re-establishment occurs.
