To log BGP neighbor state changes (up/down events) for the "prod_grp" group, use the following commands:  

```  
configure  
router bgp  
 group prod_grp  
  log-change  
```  

This configuration enables logging of session state transitions for all neighbors in "prod_grp". The logs will record connection/disconnection events, which can be viewed via the router's syslog or debugging outputs for troubleshooting.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Trying to track when devices in our "prod_grp" neighbor cluster on the Huawei NE40E flip between connected and disconnected states—how do I get the router to record those ups and downs in a log for troubleshooting?
---
## Proposed answer:
To log BGP neighbor state changes (up/down events) for the "prod_grp" group, use the following commands:  

```  
configure  
router bgp  
 group prod_grp  
  log-change  
```  

This configuration enables logging of session state transitions for all neighbors in "prod_grp". The logs will record connection/disconnection events, which can be viewed via the router's syslog or debugging outputs for troubleshooting.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> log-change
undo peer <group-name> log-change
FuncDef:
The peer log-change command enables a BGP device to log the session status and events of a specified group.
The undo peer log-change command cancels the configuration.
By default, a BGP device is enabled to log the session status and events of a specified peer group.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
---
