To configure BGP on your Huawei NE40E to cap L2VPN routes at 50k, generate a warning at 80% capacity, and terminate the session with a 60-minute idle timeout upon exceeding the limit, use the following commands:

```bash
bgp
 group l2vpn-peers
  prefix-limit l2-vpn 50000 threshold 80 idle-timeout 60
```

### Explanation:
- **`prefix-limit l2-vpn 50000`**: Sets a maximum limit of 50,000 L2VPN address-discovery routes.
- **`threshold 80`**: Triggers a syslog warning when the route count reaches 80% of the limit (40,000 routes).
- **`idle-timeout 60`**: Automatically terminates the BGP session for 60 minutes if the route count exceeds 50,000. The session will automatically re-establish after this period.
