## Proposed answer:
To resolve the issue of your BGP VPNv4 neighbor group "VPN_GROUP" advertising routes with internal AS tags, apply the following configuration:

```
configure terminal
router bgp
 group VPN_GROUP
  remove-private
```

This command removes private AS numbers from the AS path when advertising routes to peers in "VPN_GROUP". It specifically scrubs internal-only AS markers while preserving your group's AS identifier. The configuration operates at the group level, ensuring consistent behavior for all neighbors in "VPN_GROUP".
