```
configure router
    bgp
        enable-inter-as-vpn
        group "bgp_vpn_peers"
            neighbor <peer_ip_1>
            neighbor <peer_ip_2>
            neighbor <peer_ip_3>
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Replace `<peer_ip_1>`, `<peer_ip_2>`, etc. with your actual peer IP addresses.**  
This configuration:  
1. Enables Inter-AS VPN (Option B) for cross-AS VPN route exchange (`enable-inter-as-vpn`)  
2. Creates a BGP peer group named "bgp_vpn_peers"  
3. Adds all specified VPN peers to the group using `neighbor` commands  

For route encryption, ensure IPsec/MPLS encryption is configured separately on the interfaces to these peers.
