## User question:
Hey folks, on a Huawei NE40E box, I’ve got a bunch of VPNv4 BGP neighbors grouped under "customer_group" for a multi-site setup. They’re connected via route reflectors, but I’m worried about routes learned from these peers getting boomeranged back to them. Any trick to tweak the group config so updates don’t loop back to the original sender?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent VPNv4 BGP routes from being reflected back to the originating peers in your "customer_group" on the Huawei NE40E, use the following configuration:

```cli
system-view
bgp <your_as_number>
 group customer_group
  disable-client-reflect
```

This command disables route reflection from the route reflector to clients within "customer_group", eliminating the risk of route boomeranging while maintaining other reflection behaviors.
