To allow BGP routes from the "hub_peers" group with your AS number appearing up to three times in the AS_PATH, use the following configuration. This adjusts the loop detection threshold to permit the routes without modification or flapping:

```cli
bgp
  group hub_peers
  ipv4-family unicast
    peer allow-as-loop 3
```

**Explanation:**  
- `peer allow-as-loop 3` explicitly permits routes containing your local AS number up to **three times** in the AS_PATH. This overrides the default loop prevention behavior that rejects routes with your AS appearing even once. Apply this under the IPv4 unicast family settings for the "hub_peers" group.
