## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E running IPv6 BGP unicast, if I have a group of neighbors called "ipv6_peers," what’s the trick to make the router ignore those optional route tagging details that come with updates—like those extra parameters some devices add—so they don’t mess with our path selection?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the Huawei NE40E to ignore optional extended community attributes in BGP updates for the "ipv6_peers" group, use the following commands:

```
config>router>bgp>group>ipv6_peers
    disable-communities extended
exit
```

This command removes extended communities from updates sent to the group, ensuring they are not processed or used in path selection.
