Based on your requirement to attach bandwidth tags to incoming VPNv4 routes from the "dc_backbone" neighbor group for downstream propagation, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "dc_backbone"
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP group context for "dc_backbone"
2. Enables link-bandwidth handling for the group
3. Automatically adds link-bandwidth extended communities to IPv4 routes received from directly connected EBGP peers in this group

The link-bandwidth extended community will be attached to eligible routes received from the backbone peers, making these bandwidth tags available for downstream propagation decisions.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
