## Proposed answer:
To configure the Huawei NE40E to share BGP-specific route tags (extended communities) with the "bgp_group1" group for regular IPv6 routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
config router bgp
group "bgp_group1"
link-bandwidth
send-to-ebgp ipv6
exit
exit
exit
```

This configuration enables the handling of the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes and ensures it is advertised to EBGP peers in "bgp_group1".
