## User question:
If I'm setting up a multicast setup over VPNv4 on a Huawei NE40E box and have a BGP group called "bgp_mcast_peers," how do I make sure routes received from those peers don't get accidentally sent back to them through reflections, like maybe using some kind of tagging trick or tweaking group policies? Trying to avoid routing loops in this shared multicast environment.
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent routes received from BGP peers in the "bgp_mcast_peers" group from being reflected back to them, configure the `disable-client-reflect` command under the group. This ensures routes learned from these peers are not readvertised to them via reflection, avoiding potential routing loops:

```cli
config>router>bgp
    group "bgp_mcast_peers"
        disable-client-reflect
    exit
exit
