To ensure your Huawei NE40E uses its own address as the next-hop gateway when sharing routes with iBGP peers in the "vpn_core" group, apply the following configuration:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group "vpn_core"
            next-hop-self
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
The `next-hop-self` command forces the router to advertise itself as the next-hop gateway to all peers in the specified BGP group ("vpn_core" in your case). This overrides the default iBGP behavior where the next-hop address remains unchanged from the original route advertisement.
