## Proposed answer:
To prioritize routes from your BGP "VPN-PEERS" group for VPN-specific traffic by setting a higher local-preference of 200, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
config router bgp
 group "VPN-PEERS"
  local-preference 200
```

This command applies the local-preference value directly to the group, ensuring all routes received from peers in "VPN-PEERS" are assigned a higher preference (200) within your BGP path selection process.
