User input:

Hey, I'm working with a Huawei NE40E and need to set it up so inbound LSP tunnels are only built for BGP routes that carry MPLS tags and get approved by our existing route policy named "lsp-filter-1"—want to make sure it doesn’t create those paths for anything else. How do I lock this down in the config?

To configure conditional advertisement of a default route to BGP group "ISP_Backbone" neighbors only when the prefixes 192.168.10.0/24 or 203.179.25.128/25 exist in the routing table:

```cli
ip ip-prefix PL_PREFIX1 index 10 permit 192.168.10.0 24
ip ip-prefix PL_PREFIX2 index 10 permit 203.179.25.128 25
track 1
  type route ip-prefix PL_PREFIX1
track 2
  type route ip-prefix PL_PREFIX2
track-group 1
  mode or
  object 1
  object 2
ip route-static 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 Null0 track track-group 1
ip ip-prefix DEFAULT_ROUTE index 10 permit 0.0.0.0 0
route-policy RP_REDISTRIBUTE_DEFAULT permit node 10
  if-match ip-prefix DEFAULT_ROUTE
router bgp
  group ISP_Backbone
  import-route static route-policy RP_REDISTRIBUTE_DEFAULT
```

**Explanation:**  
- Track objects monitor the presence of each prefix in the routing table.  
- Track-group 1 uses logical OR to trigger when either prefix is present.  
- The static default route is activated only if the track-group condition is satisfied.  
- Route policy `RP_REDISTRIBUTE_DEFAULT` allows redistribution of only the default route into BGP.  
- The static route is redistributed into BGP and advertised to "ISP_Backbone" neighbors only when the static route is active (i.e., when either prefix exists).
