## User question:
Hey, I’m setting up a VPN setup on a Huawei NE40E and want to limit what routes my BGP neighbor group "VPN_PEERS" can see. I’ve got a custom policy template named "VPN_FILTER" ready—how do I tie it specifically to the VPNv4 section to make sure only certain routes get shared?
---
## Proposed answer:
To limit the routes for your BGP neighbor group "VPN_PEERS" using the policy "VPN_FILTER" specifically for VPNv4, configure the following commands:

```cli
configure
router bgp
 group VPN_PEERS
  import policy VPN_FILTER
  vpn-apply-import
```

This applies the "VPN_FILTER" policy to VPNv4 routes, ensuring only the routes defined in the policy are shared with the group.
