## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
group <group-name> listen { internal | external | confederation-external }
group <group-name> listen
undo group <group-name> listen [ internal | external | confederation-external ]
FuncDef:
The group listen command creates a dynamic BGP peer group.
The undo group listen command deletes a dynamic BGP peer group.
By default, no dynamic BGP peer groups are created.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a dynamic BGP peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'internal', 'Info': 'Creates a dynamic IBGP peer group.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'external', 'Info': 'Creates a dynamic EBGP peer group.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'confederation-external', 'Info': 'Creates a dynamic confederation EBGP peer group.\n-'}
