To prevent routes learned from a neighbor in the BGP group "mvpn_peers" from being reflected back to the same neighbor, use the `disable-client-reflect` command applied at the neighbor level. This ensures routes received from a specific neighbor are not advertised back to it while still allowing reflection to other clients in the group.

```cli
configure terminal
router bgp
 group mvpn_peers
  neighbor <neighbor_ip>
   disable-client-reflect
  exit
 exit
exit
```

Replace `<neighbor_ip>` with the IP address of each neighbor in the "mvpn_peers" group. Repeat the `neighbor <neighbor_ip>` and `disable-client-reflect` configuration for every neighbor in the group to enforce this behavior universally.
