To ensure only IPv6 networks in `PREF_LIST_1` are advertised to `GROUP_A` peers and block all others, configure an export route policy and apply it to the group:

```cli
ip ipv6-prefix PREF_LIST_1 index 10 permit <network> <mask>
  ! Repeat for each allowed IPv6 network
!
route-policy ALLOW_PREF_LIST_1 permit node 10
  if-match ipv6-prefix PREF_LIST_1
!
route-policy ALLOW_PREF_LIST_1 deny node 20
  ! Blocks all other routes
!
router bgp
  group GROUP_A
    ipv6-family unicast
      export route-policy ALLOW_PREF_LIST_1
```

**Explanation:**  
- **`ip ipv6-prefix`**: Defines the IPv6 networks permitted for advertisement (`PREF_LIST_1`).  
- **`route-policy`**:  
  - **`node 10`**: Permits routes matching `PREF_LIST_1`.  
  - **`node 20`**: Implicitly denies all other routes.  
- **`export route-policy`**: Applies the policy to `GROUP_A` under `ipv6-family unicast`, ensuring only the allowed IPv6 networks are advertised.  

**Verification**:  
After configuration, check advertised routes to `GROUP_A` peers:  
```cli
display bgp ipv6 peer GROUP_A advertised-routes
```
