To filter incoming MVPNv6 routes from the BGP neighbor group "mvpn-group1" using the rule-set "rp_mvpn_filter," apply the following configuration:

```cli
config
   router bgp [AS_Number]
      group mvpn-group1
         vpn-apply-import
```

### Explanation:
- **`vpn-apply-import`** enables the base BGP import route policy (in this case, your predefined rule-set "rp_mvpn_filter") to filter routes for MVPNv6 (and other VPN address families). This command must be applied directly to the BGP neighbor group "mvpn-group1".

### Key Notes:
1. Ensure **`rp_mvpn_filter`** is already configured as a valid import route policy in the base BGP instance (IPv4/IPv6 unicast context).
2. The policy will automatically filter MVPNv6 routes received from peers in "mvpn-group1" once applied.
3. Replace `[AS_Number]` with your BGP autonomous system number.

This configuration leverages the referenced `vpn-apply-import` command to enforce your rule-set on MVPNv6 routes.
