## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E box, I need to make sure only specific routes get shared with my BGP neighbors grouped as "internet_peers"—like blocking some prefixes from accidentally leaking out. There's an existing policy named "filter_internet" meant for this. How do I hook that up properly for outbound updates?
---
## Proposed answer:
To apply the existing "filter_internet" policy for outbound BGP updates to the "internet_peers" group, use the following configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
group internet_peers
 outbound-route-filtering
  extended-community
   send-orf filter_internet
```

These commands enable outbound route filtering at the group level, specify extended community-based filtering, and apply the "filter_internet" policy to control advertised routes.
