To configure the NE40E so it advertises its own interface IP as the next-hop for routes sent to the IBGP group `internal_peers`, use the following commands:

```cli
system-view
bgp <as_number>
group internal_peers
next-hop-self
commit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`system-view`**: Enters configuration mode.  
2. **`bgp <as_number>`**: Enters BGP configuration context (replace `<as_number>` with your BGP AS).  
3. **`group internal_peers`**: Specifies the IBGP peer group `internal_peers`.  
4. **`next-hop-self`**: Forces the router to use its own interface IP as the next-hop address for all routes advertised to this group.  
5. **`commit`**: Applies the configuration changes.  

This ensures traffic to the advertised routes passes through this router.
