To configure a hard limit of 500 seconds for BGP neighbors that are slow in exchanging routing updates, use the `hold-time` command to set both the proposed hold time and the minimum acceptable hold time to 500 seconds. Apply this configuration at the appropriate level (global BGP, group, or neighbor):

```cli
<system-view>
[~HUAWEI] bgp <as-number>
[*HUAWEI-bgp] hold-time 500 min 500
```

Replace `<as-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number. This configuration ensures:
- The router proposes a 500-second hold time to neighbors.
- Only neighbors accepting a hold time of at least 500 seconds can establish sessions.
- Sessions with neighbors failing to respond within 500 seconds will be terminated.
