To allow BGP routes with your own AS appearing up to three times in the AS path for the "hub_spoke" group, configure the following:

```cli
config>router>bgp>group hub_spoke
 loop-detect off
```

This disables AS path loop detection for the group, permitting routes with repeated AS numbers (including your own AS up to three times). Ensure this aligns with your network's security policies, as it allows any number of AS path repetitions.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E box running BGP with VPN target filtering, I've got a hub-spoke group called "hub_spoke" sending us routes. How do I tweak the config to allow paths where our own AS number shows up max three times in the AS path—like maybe duplicated or looped a couple times—without the router rejecting them? Trying to handle some weird path scenarios but not open security holes.
---
## Proposed answer:
To allow BGP routes with your own AS appearing up to three times in the AS path for the "hub_spoke" group, configure the following:

```cli
config>router>bgp>group hub_spoke
 loop-detect off
```

This disables AS path loop detection for the group, permitting routes with repeated AS numbers (including your own AS up to three times). Ensure this aligns with your network's security policies, as it allows any number of AS path repetitions.
---
