On a Huawei NE40E, when setting up VPLS to connect two sites, where exactly do I go in BGP to enable the part that lets them swap member details? I’m stuck in the config menus and can’t find the right spot.

To configure the Huawei NE40E as a central route reflector for the "internet_peers" BGP group handling standard IPv4 routes without typical path-hinting attributes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "internet_peers"
            dynamic-neighbor
            exit
        optimal-route-reflection
            location 1
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `dynamic-neighbor` command enables dynamic BGP sessions within the "internet_peers" group to handle multiple ISP peers efficiently.  
- The `optimal-route-reflection` context with `location 1` configures the router as a route reflector, optimizing path selection without relying on conventional attributes.  

Ensure all ISP peers are defined under the "internet_peers" group using the `neighbor <ip-address>` command (replace `<ip-address>` with actual peer IPs). No additional path-hinting attributes are required.
