To prevent the router from modifying the next-hop information when advertising VPNv6 routes to external peers in the `inter_as_group`, use the following configuration:

```bash
configure router bgp
    group "inter_as_group"
        next-hop-unchanged
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6
```

This ensures:
- `next-hop-unchanged` preserves the original next-hop for all routes advertised to the group
- `advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6` explicitly enables proper IPv6 next-hop handling for VPNv6 routes, maintaining the actual source hop across autonomous systems.
