Hey, I’ve got a Huawei NE40E where I need to stop certain labeled BGP routes coming from my core network group "CORE_GROUP" unless they match a simple access list (ID 2100). How do I set this up so it only accepts the allowed path updates? Trying to avoid unwanted route injections here.

To ensure incoming label paths are built only for BGP routes with MPLS tags that pass the "customer-vpn" access list, configure the following:

```cli
router bgp <AS-number>
 neighbor <neighbor-ip>
  family label-ipv4
   import customer-vpn
   exit
  exit
 exit
```

Replace `<AS-number>` with your BGP autonomous system number and `<neighbor-ip>` with the specific BGP neighbor IP address. This applies the "customer-vpn" policy to filter incoming labeled IPv4 routes at the ingress.
