To block unwanted BGP routes to the peer at 192.168.1.1 using your existing filter `CUSTOM_FILTER`, apply the following configuration:  

```  
configure  
router bgp  
 group [GROUP_NAME]  
  neighbor 192.168.1.1  
   outbound-route-filtering  
    extended-community  
     send-orf CUSTOM_FILTER  
   exit  
  exit  
 exit  
exit  
```  

Replace `[GROUP_NAME]` with the BGP group containing this neighbor. This configures extended-community-based ORF to send your `CUSTOM_FILTER` to the peer, preventing announcements of routes matching the filter.
