User input:

Hey, I’ve got a Huawei NE40E setup where I’m passing BGP routes with MPLS labels to an internal neighbor at 192.168.10.5, but it’s messing with the next-hop info. How do I stop the router from altering that specific detail when sharing those routes?

To ensure the router verifies tunnel status before advertising labeled routes to neighbor 192.168.5.5, configure BGP next-hop resolution to strictly use only tagged LSPs. This forces the router to consider only operational tunnels with an admin tag for next-hop resolution.

```
configure router bgp
  next-hop-resolution
    labeled-routes
      transport-tunnel
        family ipv4
          enforce-strict-tunnel-tagging
        exit
      exit
