To set up BGP origin validation for regular IPv4 traffic on your Huawei NE40E, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure
router bgp
 best-path-selection
  origin-invalid-unusable
 exit
 group <GROUP_NAME>
  enable-origin-validation ipv4
 exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `origin-invalid-unusable` marks routes with an `Invalid` origin validation state as unusable (not used for forwarding or advertisement).  
- `enable-origin-validation ipv4` enables certificate-based origin validation for IPv4 routes received from neighbors in the specified BGP group.  

Replace `<GROUP_NAME>` with your actual BGP group name. This ensures IPv4 routes from neighbors in this group are validated against RPKI certificates, and invalid routes are discarded.
