To adjust the BGP reconnect behavior for the neighbor 192.168.5.8 without affecting the remote peer's perception, configure the `connect-retry` timer to 300 seconds (5 minutes) specifically for that neighbor:

```cli
system-view
bgp [your-local-as-number]
peer 192.168.5.8 connect-retry 300
commit
```

Replace `[your-local-as-number]` with your router's BGP AS number. This change only affects local reconnection attempts and is not visible to the remote peer.
