To configure your Huawei NE40E to advertise inactive BGP routes (backup paths) to the peer at 192.168.10.5, use the following commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
  neighbor 192.168.10.5
    advertise-inactive
  exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
The `advertise-inactive` command enables advertising BGP routes that are not the most preferred (inactive) to the specified neighbor. This ensures your peer receives backup paths alongside the primary best routes.
