To address the issue where IPv6 BGP routes aren't using the default route as a backup when the direct next-hop is unreachable, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
   next-hop-res
      use-bgp-routes
   exit
   backup-path ipv6
exit
```

This enables recursive next-hop resolution using BGP routes (including the default route) and activates fast reroute for unlabeled IPv6 BGP routes to switch to backup paths during next-hop failures.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
Hey, I’ve got an NE40E box where IPv6 BGP routes aren’t using the catch-all gateway as a backup path when the immediate next-hop is unreachable. How do I tweak the v6 unicast settings so it leans on the default route in those cases? It’s causing some paths to drop when direct connections flap.
---
## Proposed answer:
To address the issue where IPv6 BGP routes aren't using the default route as a backup when the direct next-hop is unreachable, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
   next-hop-res
      use-bgp-routes
   exit
   backup-path ipv6
exit
```

This enables recursive next-hop resolution using BGP routes (including the default route) and activates fast reroute for unlabeled IPv6 BGP routes to switch to backup paths during next-hop failures.
---
