To address the sluggish nodes in your Layer 2 BGP group, configure the hold timer to automatically quarantine neighbors lagging by more than 4 minutes (240 seconds). Use these commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "L2_GROUP"
        hold-time 240 min 240
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `hold-time 240` sets the maximum interval between BGP keepalive/update messages to 240 seconds (4 minutes).  
- `min 240` enforces that peers must accept a minimum hold time of 240 seconds during session negotiation.  
- If a neighbor fails to send a keepalive/update within 240 seconds, the session is automatically torn down ("quarantined").  
- Apply this to your Layer 2 BGP group (replace `"L2_GROUP"` with your actual group name).  

For specific neighbors, configure under the neighbor instead:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "L2_GROUP"
        neighbor <IP_ADDRESS>
            hold-time 240 min 240
        exit
    exit
exit
```
