To configure the router to wait up to 5 minutes (300 seconds) for the "INTERNAL_PEERS" neighbor connections during BGP restart recovery, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
 bgp
  group "INTERNAL_PEERS"
   graceful-restart
    stale-routes-time 300
   exit
  exit
 exit
exit
```

This sets the maximum time stale routes are maintained after a graceful restart to 300 seconds for the specified peer group.
