## Proposed answer:
To set up BGP instance 200 for IPv6 unicast routing on the Huawei NE40E, use the following configuration commands:

```cli
router
    bgp 200
        family ipv6
```

This enables the unlabeled IPv6 unicast address family for BGP instance 200. To exchange routes, you must also activate the IPv6 family for relevant neighbors or groups. For example:

```cli
    group <GROUP_NAME>
        family ipv6
    neighbor <NEIGHBOR_IP>
        family ipv6
```

Replace `<GROUP_NAME>` and `<NEIGHBOR_IP>` with your specific group name and neighbor IP address. Ensure IPv6 connectivity and proper BGP peering are established.
