User input:

On a Huawei NE40E, I need to pass along those extended community tags with the bigger format to my BGP neighbor at 192.168.5.10, specifically within the multicast-related routing context. Tried some commands but they aren't sticking—what's the right way to set this up?

To configure the Huawei NE40E as a central hub mirroring IPv6 VPN routes for 'client_group1' using BGP route reflection:

```cli
bgp <as-number>
  group client_group1 internal
    peer client_group1 enable
    peer client_group1 reflect-client
    neighbor <client-ip1>
    neighbor <client-ip2>
    neighbor <client-ipN>
  ipv6-family vpnv6
    peer client_group1 enable
```

Replace `<as-number>` with your BGP AS number and `<client-ip1>`, `<client-ip2>`, etc., with the IPv6 addresses of the client routers in the group. This configuration:
- Creates a BGP group 'client_group1'
- Enables route reflection for all clients in the group
- Adds client neighbors efficiently without per-neighbor duplication
- Activates IPv6 VPN route mirroring for the group

Key optimizations:
- `peer reflect-client` applied at group level avoids per-neighbor duplication
- Group-based IPv6 VPN activation simplifies configuration
- Internal group type assumes clients share the same AS as the hub
