To configure the Huawei NE40E for IPv6 BGP route passthrough without altering routes between external providers in the "internet_peers" group, use these commands:

```cli
bgp <your_AS_number>
 group internet_peers
  no disable-client-reflect
  neighbor <provider1_IPv6_address>
   no disable-client-reflect
  neighbor <provider2_IPv6_address>
   no disable-client-reflect
  ! Repeat for additional providers
```

**Key notes:**
1. Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your BGP autonomous system number
2. Replace `<provider1_IPv6_address>`, `<provider2_IPv6_address>`, etc., with actual peer IPv6 addresses
3. Ensure all peers are first configured under the group using `neighbor <ipv6-address>`
4. The `no disable-client-reflect` commands must be applied at both the group level and individual neighbor level for consistent behavior

This configuration ensures received routes are transparently reflected between all providers in the group without modification. No route policies or additional attributes are applied.
