Your answer:

To propagate BGP origin AS validation status to your neighbor at 192.168.5.5 without extended communities, configure Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) to signal validation results via prefix-based filtering:

```cli
configure
router bgp
 group <your-group-name>
  neighbor 192.168.5.5
   outbound-route-filtering
    extended-community
     accept-orf
    exit
   exit
  exit
 exit
exit
```

**Key notes:**  
1. Replace `<your-group-name>` with your BGP group name.  
2. This enables ORF negotiation to accept/apply prefix filters from the neighbor.  
3. Combine this with local prefix policies that tag valid/invalid routes (e.g., using communities or AS-path filters). The neighbor will implicitly infer validation status through route acceptance/withdrawal.  

**Alternative approach:** Withdraw invalid routes from the neighbor entirely using route policies, as BGP withdrawals inherently signal invalid states.
