To address the slow BGP neighbors handling VPNv4 multicast traffic and set the hold time to 200 seconds, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
 neighbor <neighbor-ip>
  hold-time 200 min 200
 exit
exit
```

Replace `<neighbor-ip>` with the specific neighbor IP addresses or apply this configuration to the relevant BGP group if multiple neighbors require the same settings. This ensures sessions wait 200 seconds before termination and rejects any peer proposing a hold time below 200 seconds.
