To configure your Huawei NE40E for exchanging multiple path details with the BGP group "internal-peers" for labeled routes, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure
router
 bgp
  group "internal-peers"
   add-paths
    label-ipv4 send 4 receive
    label-ipv6 send 4 receive
   exit
  exit
 exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
- **`label-ipv4 send 4 receive`**: Enables sending (up to 4 paths) and receiving labeled IPv4 routes.
- **`label-ipv6 send 4 receive`**: Enables sending (up to 4 paths) and receiving labeled IPv6 routes.
- Adjust the `send` value (4 in this example) between 1-16 as needed for your topology.
- These commands apply to the BGP group "internal-peers" to exchange multiple path options for labeled routes.
