User input:

I'm working with a Huawei NE40E handling multicast routing over BGP and getting false alerts about neighbors being too slow during MDT route exchanges—how do I turn off that strict "you're lagging" monitoring that uses absolute thresholds instead of relative calculations?

To prevent the router from altering the next-hop information when sharing BGP routes with MPLS labels to the neighbor at 192.168.10.5, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    neighbor 192.168.10.5
        next-hop-unchanged label-ipv4
    exit
exit
```

This command ensures the next-hop remains unchanged for labeled IPv4 routes sent to the specified neighbor.
