Hey, I'm working with a Huawei NE40E where I need to set up route reflection for multicast traffic groups using BGP. Specifically, I want to apply filter #25 tied to VPN-Target's tagging system in the MDT routing setup. How do I nail the policy setup for reflecting these routes correctly?

! The feature you need is "BGP keep-all-routes," which retains all received paths. Here's the configuration:

config router bgp  
 group <group-name>  
  neighbor <neighbor-ip>  
   keep-all-routes  
  exit  
 exit  
exit  

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the neighbor's IP address. This preserves all received routes even if filtered, and won't require session resets during policy changes.
