To ensure your Huawei NE40E advertises only EVPN/VPN routes with RT attributes accepted by a specific BGP neighbor, configure Outbound Route Filtering (ORF) for extended communities (route targets) on that peer:

```
peer <peer-ip>
 outbound-route-filtering
  extended-community
   accept-orf
```

Replace `<peer-ip>` with the neighbor's IP address. This configuration:
1. Enables ORF under the peer configuration
2. Activates extended community filtering (for route targets)
3. Allows the router to accept and apply the neighbor's RT-based filter preferences

The neighbor must support sending ORF requests. After capability negotiation, your router will dynamically filter advertised EVPN/VPN routes to match the peer's requested RT attributes.
