To configure BGP for IPv6 to propagate traffic priority tags (like extended communities) for tracking data usage per-class across peers on Huawei NE40E, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv6
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
1. **`link-bandwidth`** enables handling of extended communities for traffic priority tags.  
2. **`send-to-ebgp ipv6`** ensures IPv6 routes carry these tags when advertised to EBGP peers.  
3. Replace **`<group-name>`** with your BGP peer group name.  

For per-neighbor configuration (if needed):  
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv6
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```  

This setup allows extended communities (e.g., traffic priority tags) to be attached to IPv6 routes, enabling downstream per-class data usage tracking.
