```cli
route-policy POLICY_NAME permit node NODE_NUMBER
 apply extcommunity rt VPN_IDENTIFIER:ORIGIN_SITE_TAG additive
!
router bgp AS_NUMBER
 group GROUP_NAME
  family ipv4 unicast
  peer PEER_ADDRESS
   address-family ipv4-labelunicast
    policy vpn-target
    route-policy POLICY_NAME in
   exit
  exit
 exit
 exit
```

Replace `POLICY_NAME`, `NODE_NUMBER`, `VPN_IDENTIFIER`, `ORIGIN_SITE_TAG`, `AS_NUMBER`, `GROUP_NAME`, and `PEER_ADDRESS` with your specific values. This configuration:
- Uses `apply extcommunity` in the route policy to modify VPN identifiers (Route Targets) and origin-site tags
- Applies the policy to incoming labeled unicast routes (`ipv4-labelunicast` address family)
- Preserves existing VPNv4 configurations by isolating changes to the labeled unicast table
- Uses the `additive` parameter to retain existing extended communities while appending new ones
