            exit
        exit
    group <your_group_name>
        advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6
        default-route-target
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `family vpn` under `next-hop-resolution` ensures VPNv6 routes use tunnel-based next-hop resolution.  
- `advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6` forces VPNv6 routes to use IPv6 next-hops, enabling compatibility with IPv6 default routes.  
- `default-route-target` advertises the default RTC route to peers, ensuring fallback paths are recognized when specific routes are unavailable.  

Replace `<your_group_name>` with your BGP peer group. This configuration prioritizes the default gateway when specific next-hop details are unresolved.
