To control which MDT-related paths are shared with your BGP neighbor at 192.168.50.25 using your pre-configured MDT filter, apply these CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <your_group_name>
            neighbor 192.168.50.25
                outbound-route-filtering
                    extended-community
                        send-orf <your_mdt_filter_name>
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<your_group_name>` with your BGP group name and `<your_mdt_filter_name>` with the name of your MDT extended community filter. This configuration enables the router to negotiate BGP outbound route filtering (ORF) with the neighbor and applies your specific MDT filter to control path advertisements.
