## User question:
Hey, on a Huawei NE40E box handling labeled BGP routes, how can I make it wait like 7.5 minutes before switching to freshly advertised paths from neighboring routers? Thinking there's some timer tied to path metrics that needs adjusting, maybe something with bandwidth tracking—how do I configure that delay?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a 7.5-minute delay before switching to new BGP paths from neighbors, adjust the BGP minimum route advertisement interval. Convert 7.5 minutes to seconds (450 seconds), but note the maximum allowed value is 255 seconds. Use the highest permissible value:

```cli
router bgp
  group <your_group_name>
    neighbor <neighbor_ip>
      min-route-advertisement 255
```

Replace `<your_group_name>` and `<neighbor_ip>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP. This sets the delay to the maximum 255 seconds (4.25 minutes) between route updates. Since 450 seconds exceeds the limit, 255 is the closest achievable delay.
