To configure your Huawei NE40E to send extended communities (like extra-long tags) to the BGP neighbor group INTERNET_PEERS (external peers), use these CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
 group INTERNET_PEERS
  link-bandwidth
   send-to-ebgp ipv4
```

This enables the sending of extended communities (specifically the link-bandwidth type) to eBGP peers in the INTERNET_PEERS group for IPv4 routes.
