## User question:
Hey, I’m working on a Huawei NE40E and need to configure it so that those extra-long community tags (the ones bigger than standard) get shared with my BGP neighbor group called INTERNET_PEERS—they’re external peers. How do I ensure the router actually sends those extended values to them?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure your Huawei NE40E to send extended communities (like extra-long tags) to the BGP neighbor group INTERNET_PEERS (external peers), use these CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
 group INTERNET_PEERS
  link-bandwidth
   send-to-ebgp ipv4
```

This enables the sending of extended communities (specifically the link-bandwidth type) to eBGP peers in the INTERNET_PEERS group for IPv4 routes.
