---
## Proposed answer:
To enable BGP for VPLS member exchange on the Huawei NE40E, configure the following:

```
configure
router bgp <as-number>
 group <group-name>
  neighbor <neighbor-ip>
   graceful-restart
    long-lived
     family l2-vpn
```

**Key details:**  
1. Navigate to `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart>long-lived`  
2. Use `family l2-vpn` to activate Layer 2 VPN address family exchange  
3. Replace `<as-number>`, `<group-name>`, and `<neighbor-ip>` with your BGP AS, peer group name, and neighbor IP address  

This enables the VPLS endpoint discovery and label exchange between sites. Ensure BGP peers are already defined in the group.
