---
## User question:
When setting up multi-instance VPNs on a Huawei NE40E using BGP, if I’ve got a group of peers called "bgp_peers" and want to make sure the router waits up to 500 seconds for that final "all routes sent" confirmation from them before timing out—like after a session reset where routes aren’t fully received yet—what’s the trick to adjusting that max delay specifically for the peer group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the maximum wait time for the "all routes sent" confirmation to 500 seconds for the BGP peer group "bgp_peers", use the following commands:

```cli
router bgp
 group bgp_peers
  graceful-restart
   stale-routes-time 500
   exit
  exit
 exit
```

This configuration sets the `stale-routes-time` to 500 seconds under the `graceful-restart` context for the specified peer group, ensuring the router waits up to 500 seconds for the final End-of-RIB marker after a session reset.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> local-graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib <wfrtime>
undo peer <group-name> local-graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib
FuncDef:
The peer local-graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib command sets the maximum duration for a BGP restarter to wait for the End-of-RIB flag from each peer in a specified group.
The undo peer local-graceful-restart timer wait-for-rib command deletes the configured duration.
By default, a BGP restarter waits for the End-of-RIB flag from each peer in a specified group for a maximum of 600s.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a BGP peer group.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters. If spaces are used, the string must start and end with double quotation marks (").'}
{'Parameters': 'wfrtime', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum duration for a BGP restarter to wait for the End-of-RIB flag.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 3 to 3000, in seconds.'}
---
