## User question:
On Huawei NE40E boxes, if I want all BGP neighbors in the "bb" peer group to wait up to 5 minutes (like 300 ticks) for their restart handshake to finish before giving up, how do I set that timeout globally for the entire group instead of per neighbor?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a 5-minute (300-second) restart handshake timeout for all BGP neighbors in the "bb" peer group, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure
router bgp
group "bb"
graceful-restart
restart-time 300
exit
exit
exit
```

This sets the restart-time under the graceful-restart configuration for the peer group "bb", ensuring all neighbors in the group inherit the 300-second timeout.
