## User question:
On a Huawei NE40E, if all my MDT peer group members have direct connections set up between them, how do I make the route reflector stop sharing their routes with each other? Trying to tidy up some configs where the reflector doesn’t need to handle updates between clients anymore.
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent the route reflector from sharing routes between clients in your MDT peer group, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure
router bgp <your_AS_number>
 group <MDT_group_name>
  disable-client-reflect
```

Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your BGP autonomous system number and `<MDT_group_name>` with the name of your MDT peer group. This command disables route reflection to all clients in the specified group while maintaining their client status.
