## Proposed answer:
To ensure the router does not modify the next-hop information when sending MPLS-tagged routes to your internal BGP neighbors in the "bgp_peers" group, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "bgp_peers"
            next-hop-unchanged label-ipv4
```

This command explicitly preserves the original next-hop for labeled IPv4 routes when advertising to peers in the "bgp_peers" group. If you also need to handle labeled IPv6 routes, add the `label-ipv6` parameter:

