To address your requirement of configuring the router to wait a maximum of 500 seconds for the End-of-RIB (EoR) signal from peer `192.168.50.45` during a graceful restart, use the following CLI commands:

```
bgp <as-number>
 peer 192.168.50.45
  graceful-restart
   stale-routes-time 500
   quit
  quit
 quit
```

### Explanation:
- The `stale-routes-time` command sets the maximum duration (500 seconds) the router will retain stale routes while waiting for the EoR marker from the peer during graceful restart.
- This configuration is applied directly under the neighbor's `graceful-restart` settings to ensure it affects only peer `192.168.50.45`.
- The value `500` is within the valid range (1–3600 seconds) as specified in the documentation.
