To set up BGP monitoring for all public IPv4 routes (non-multicast) and enable instant logging of path changes on your Huawei NE40E, configure the following commands. Replace `<MONITOR_GROUP>` with your BGP group name and `<MONITOR_NEIGHBOR_IP>` with the IP address of your monitoring tool.

```cli
config>router>bgp
   group <MONITOR_GROUP>
      neighbor <MONITOR_NEIGHBOR_IP>
         add-paths
            ipv4 send 16 receive none
         exit
      exit
   exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
- `ipv4 send 16 receive none` enables advertising **up to 16 paths** per IPv4 prefix to the monitoring neighbor while disabling multiple path reception.
- This ensures your monitoring tool receives all available paths for public IPv4 routes, allowing immediate detection of path changes.
- Combine this with standard BGP logging commands (e.g., `log-up-down` and `log-changes` in the BGP context) to capture real-time events.
