To configure the router to wait 5 minutes (300 seconds) before terminating the BGP session with the neighbor `2001:db8::1`, use the following commands:

```
system-view
bgp <as-number>
 peer 2001:db8::1
  hold-time 300 min 300
```

Replace `<as-number>` with your router's BGP AS number. This sets both the hold time and minimum acceptable hold time to 300 seconds, ensuring the session remains active for 5 minutes during connectivity issues.
