Hey, trying to configure a dedicated routing space for "customer_a" on a Huawei NE40E where MPLS and BGP handle the heavy lifting—how do I properly stitch this together without stepping on other clients' toes?

Based on your requirements, configure the following commands:

```
config>router>bgp
  neighbor 192.168.5.5
    vpn-apply-export
    exit
  exit
```

This configuration ensures VPN routes (including MPLS-tagged paths) are subjected to your base export policy (policy 2100) when advertising to neighbor 192.168.5.5. The MPLS label handling remains unaffected as this only filters route advertisements.

After applying this:
1. Define your route policy 2100 in `config>router>policy-options` to match and block the specific MPLS-tagged routes
2. Apply policy 2100 as an export policy to the neighbor using:
   ```
   neighbor 192.168.5.5
      export policy 2100
   ```
