To enable BGP multicast route exchange with neighbor 192.168.5.9 on your Huawei NE40E, use these commands:

```
bgp <your_AS_number>
 ipv4-family multicast
  peer 192.168.5.9 enable
```

**Explanation:**  
The neighbor 192.168.5.9 must be explicitly activated under the `ipv4-family multicast` address family to exchange multicast routes. Since the neighbor already exists in your base BGP configuration, these commands add multicast-specific routing capability to the existing peer. Replace `<your_AS_number>` with your actual BGP autonomous system number.

**Verification:**  
After applying, check multicast route reception with:  
`display bgp multicast routing-table`
