## User question:
On a Huawei NE40E, when setting up BGP for a VPN’s IPv4 routes, there’s a peer at 192.168.5.8 that occasionally drags its feet sending the "all clear" signal after exchanging routes. How do I tell the router to wait no more than 500 seconds for this confirmation before giving up and proceeding?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the router to wait no more than 500 seconds for confirmation from the BGP peer at 192.168.5.8, use the following commands:

```
peer 192.168.5.8
 hold-time 500
```

This sets the hold time to 500 seconds for the specified peer. The session will terminate if no keepalive or update message is received within this period.
