To configure the router to ignore VPN community tags for incoming multicast distribution paths in BGP updates, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure
router
 bgp
  no route-target-list
```

**Explanation:**  
The `no route-target-list` command removes all configured route target filters under BGP. This ensures incoming routes (including multicast distribution paths) are accepted regardless of VPN community tags, eliminating the blocking of routes that don't match specific tags. The command is applied globally to BGP routing updates.
