To configure a 30-second hold time for BGP peers in MVPN scenarios:

1. **Configure BGP hold time at the neighbor level**:
```
config>router>bgp
group <your_group_name>
neighbor <peer_IP_address>
hold-time 30 min 30
exit
exit
```

**Key points**:
- Sets both the desired hold time and minimum acceptable hold time to 30 seconds
- Applies specifically to problematic MVPN peers (replace `<your_group_name>` and `<peer_IP_address>` with your actual values)
- Session will automatically reset if keepalives aren't received within 30 seconds
- Affects all address families including MVPN IPv4/IPv6

**Verification command**:
```show router bgp neighbor <peer_IP>```
(Look for "Hold Time" and "Min Hold Time" values in output)
