To address the requirement of removing non-public AS identifiers from BGP updates received from neighbor 192.168.5.8 on your Huawei NE40E, apply the following configuration:

```cli
bgp
 group <your_group_name>
  neighbor 192.168.5.8
   peer-as <neighbor_AS_number>
   remove-private
  exit
 exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
The `remove-private` command strips reserved/internal AS numbers from the AS path of inbound routes **before** they are accepted into the BGP table. This ensures any non-public AS identifiers from neighbor 192.168.5.8 are removed during route processing, complying with your partner's policy. Replace `<your_group_name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor_AS_number>` with the actual AS of 192.168.5.8.
