To set a fixed 150-second hard cutoff for BGP sessions timing out due to slow neighbor responses, use the following command in the BGP configuration context for the affected neighbors or groups:

```cli
hold-time 150 min 150
```

This configuration:
- Sets the BGP hold time to 150 seconds.
- Enforces a minimum acceptable hold time of 150 seconds (rejecting sessions with lower values).
- Ensures the session terminates if no keepalive/update is received within 150 seconds.

Apply this at the appropriate level (global BGP, group, or neighbor) based on your setup. For example, for a specific neighbor:

```cli
router bgp <AS-number>
 neighbor <ip-address>
  hold-time 150 min 150
```
