To address the issue of slow BGP peers during multicast route updates and cap the allowed synchronization discrepancy at 800 seconds, apply the following CLI configuration commands:

```
router bgp <AS-number>
  group <group-name>
    neighbor <neighbor-ip>
      hold-time 800 min 800
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `hold-time 800` sets the maximum interval (800 seconds) that BGP will wait for a keepalive or update message before declaring the peer session down.  
- The `min 800` ensures the peer must accept a hold time of at least 800 seconds during session negotiation. Peers proposing a lower hold time will be rejected.  

This configuration marks peers exceeding the 800-second sync threshold as problematic, addressing lag in multicast distribution groups. Replace `<AS-number>`, `<group-name>`, and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific BGP details.
