To ensure extended community tags are passed to your BGP neighbor at 192.168.5.10 in the multicast context, use the following configuration:

```cli
config router bgp
  group <your_group_name>
    neighbor 192.168.5.10
      add-paths
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
      exit
      link-bandwidth
        send-to-ebgp ipv4
      exit
    exit
  exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive` enables extended community transmission for multicast VPN IPv4 routes, allowing multiple paths (`send 8` sets the path limit).  
- `send-to-ebgp ipv4` ensures link-bandwidth extended communities are propagated for IPv4 routes (adjust if using IPv6).  

Replace `<your_group_name>` with the BGP group containing the neighbor. This configuration applies to both IBGP/EBGP peers and retains extended communities in multicast updates.
