To resolve the issue with BGP neighbors not exchanging MDT multicast routes, configure the following commands:

```cli
config>router>bgp
    group <mcast-group-name>
        family mvpn-ipv4
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**  
- Replace `<mcast-group-name>` with your actual BGP group name containing the multicast neighbors.  
- The `family mvpn-ipv4` command enables the multicast VPN IPv4 address family for all neighbors in the specified group, allowing them to exchange MDT routes.  
- Ensure this configuration is applied consistently to all relevant routers participating in the MDT.  

If per-neighbor configuration is preferred instead of group-level:  
```cli
config>router>bgp
    group <mcast-group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            family mvpn-ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```
