To configure the BGP VPN setup on the Huawei NE40E to wait a maximum of five minutes (300 seconds) for neighbors in the "bb" group to reconnect after dropping, apply the following commands:

```cli
group bb
 graceful-restart
  restart-time 300
  stale-routes-time 300
```

### Explanation:
- **`group bb`**: Enters configuration mode for the BGP group named "bb".
- **`graceful-restart`**: Enables graceful restart capabilities for the group.
- **`restart-time 300`**: Sets the maximum wait time to 300 seconds (5 minutes) for neighbors to re-establish the BGP session after a restart.
- **`stale-routes-time 300`**: Retains stale routes for 300 seconds (5 minutes) during neighbor recovery, ensuring continuity while waiting for neighbors to come back online.
